window.PULSE_CURRENT = {"asOf":"2026-11-25T04:30:00Z","calendar":[{"date":"2026-11-24","event":"Printed: PBoC Hong Kong bills sold at 1.32% (3-month, CNY 20B) and 1.41% (1-year, CNY 30B); fix 6.7111 (+9 pips), 16:30 close 6.6648 (−5 pips); CSI 300 +0.14% to 3,963.82 with 3,498 stocks down; Hang Seng −0.73% to 22,219.65, a sixth fall; MOFCOM dual-use suspension extended to 27 Jan 2027; Chen Jining under investigation; US consumer confidence 103.3 (+11.4)","why":"The package rally faded on day two; the policy news was trade and politics, not demand"},{"date":"2026-11-25","event":"PBoC CNY 800B 1-year MLF (against CNY 1T maturing) and CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo, with CNY 516B of overnight repos and CNY 80B of treasury cash deposits maturing and reserves settling; fix 6.7088 (+23 pips); Shenzhou-24 launch at 08:18 with the first foreign crew member; Xiaomi results call; US October PCE price index, October consumer spending and the Q3 GDP revision; US markets closed 26 Nov (Thanksgiving) with a half session on 27 Nov","why":"The month-end funding test: whether DR001 (1.2739% on 24 Nov) holds within 5 bp of 1.25% and the 10-year stays in 1.55% to 1.60% through a CNY 500B medium-term drain for November; the December FOMC pricing (about 97% for a hike) after US PCE"},{"date":"2026-11-25","event":"US October PCE price index, October consumer spending and the Q3 GDP revision; US markets closed 26 Nov (Thanksgiving) with a half session on 27 Nov","why":"The December FOMC pricing after Williams said the Fed still has work to do; the US 10-year at 4.9218% sets the gap to the CGB"},{"date":"2026-11-27","event":"October industrial profits","why":"Whether downstream losses widen with PPI at 5.7% and output slowing to 4.8%; September +14.4%."},{"date":"2026-11-28","event":"MOFCOM suspension of the dual-use export ban to the US (gallium, germanium, antimony, superhard materials; stricter graphite review) takes effect, running to 27 Jan 2027","why":"Keeps the critical-minerals channel open past the 10 Jan truce date; any US reciprocal step on chips or tariffs is the thing to watch"},{"date":"2026-11-30","event":"November NBS PMIs","why":"Manufacturing prior 49.3, new orders 49.4, non-manufacturing 49.7, construction 48.0; new orders back above 50 would reopen the Recovery case, manufacturing below 49 would raise the Contraction question."},{"date":"2026-11-30","event":"Margin-financing minimum ratio cut from 100% to 80% takes effect on the Shanghai, Shenzhen and Beijing exchanges (same day as the NBS PMIs)","why":"Xinhua cites a theoretical CNY 400B of incremental money; whether margin balances turn up from CNY 2,134.81B (23 Nov, −CNY 8.99B on the day) is the test of the 22 Nov package"},{"date":"2026-12-01","event":"NDRC outbound investment management measures take effect","why":"Adds reporting of significant adverse developments and overseas reinvestment for Chinese outbound investors"},{"date":"2026-12-01","event":"November RatingDog manufacturing PMI","why":"Prior 52.0; whether the exporter survey holds above 51 while the official index sits at 49.3 and export delivery value grows 18.6%"},{"date":"2026-12-01","event":"EU temporary safeguard measures on hybrid vehicles (preliminary finding of 24 Nov)","why":"MOFCOM reserved WTO dispute settlement and trade compensation; exports to the EU rose 24.4% y/y in October with autos the fastest-growing line"},{"date":"2026-12-03","event":"November RatingDog services PMI","why":"Prior 50.8; a print below 50 would put the private services survey in contraction for the first time in nearly four years, with the services production index already slowing to 4.6%"},{"date":"2026-12-04","event":"Hang Seng index changes implemented after the close (effective 7 Dec)","why":"Hang Seng Tech widened from 30 to 50 stocks with Guangfa estimating about HK$29.1B of passive demand; HSCEI adds Zhipu and MiniMax"},{"date":"2026-12-07","event":"Hang Seng index changes take effect","why":"Hang Seng Index unchanged at 95; HSCEI adds Zhipu and MiniMax, drops PSBC and Shenzhou; Hang Seng Tech index 30 to 50 constituents (CATL, Luxshare, Victory Giant, Innolight, Montage, YOFC, Kingsoft Cloud, Biren and others), 8% cap"},{"date":"2026-12-08","event":"November trade","why":"Prior exports +35.2%, imports +41.6%; Dongfang Jincheng expects exports to stay above 20%; the first full month after the truce extension and the BIS remote-access rule"},{"date":"2026-12-08","event":"Vanke 22 Vanke MTN004 second holder meeting on extension terms (CNY 1.199B outstanding; record date 7 Dec, votes by 17:00 on 10 Dec, principal due 15 Dec)","why":"Vanke's first dated public extension vote after a year of implied extensions; the Huafa curve shows how the market prices a failed one"},{"date":"2026-12-09","event":"FOMC decision (US)","why":"A 25 bp hike is priced near 97% after the discount-rate minutes showed eight of twelve reserve banks asking for 4.25%; the US 10-year at 4.9038% is about 332 bp above the CGB; JPMorgan expects three hikes to 4.50% to 4.75%"},{"date":"2026-12-09","event":"November CPI and PPI","why":"Prior CPI 0.7%, PPI 5.7%; whether the m/m PPI slowdown and the oil and metals fall show in the y/y, and whether food stops falling with retail sales at 0.4%"},{"date":"2026-12-12","event":"November credit (approximate; PBoC releases between the 10th and 15th)","why":"Prior TSF 7.2%, M2 7.1%, loans 4.7%; whether household loans turn positive after −CNY 430B in October"},{"date":"2026-12-14","event":"G20 summit in Miami (14 to 15 Dec); Xi and Trump reported to plan a fourth meeting this year","why":"The next chance for tariff, chip or purchase terms before the 10 Jan 2027 truce expiry; the 24 Nov minerals extension runs to 27 Jan"},{"date":"2026-12-15","event":"November activity data and 70-city prices (approximate; NBS mid-month)","why":"Prior industrial production 4.8%, retail sales 0.4%, FAI −8.1%, unemployment 5.1%, home prices −2.4%; Dongfang Jincheng expects industrial production near 5.0%, retail sales near 1.6% and property −22%; the December Politburo meeting and the Central Economic Work Conference usually fall in the same fortnight (dates not announced)"},{"date":"2026-12-21","event":"December LPR fixing","why":"A 19th hold is the base case after Wang Qing's 2027 call; Dong Ximiao sees a small cut as possible after the Central Economic Work Conference"}],"cb":{"label":"Easing","note":"The 1-year LPR was held at 3.00% and the 5-year at 3.50% on 20 Nov, an 18th month unchanged since the 10 bp cut of May 2025, with Wang Qing of Dongfang Jincheng putting a 10 to 20 bp policy-rate cut in 2027 and Dong Ximiao of Zhaolian not ruling out a small cut around year-end. The instrument is still easing by price and the quantity is being managed into month-end: on 24 Nov the PBoC lent CNY 516B overnight at 1.25% against CNY 499.5B maturing, a CNY 16.5B net injection, and announced for 25 Nov a CNY 800B 1-year MLF against CNY 1T maturing (a CNY 200B reduction, the medium-term tools netting a CNY 500B drain in November with outright reverse repos already cut by CNY 300B) plus a CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo, the first 7-day operation since the overnight rate became the anchor, sized to cover month-end; CNY 516B of overnight repos and CNY 80B of treasury cash deposits also mature on 25 Nov, a reserve-settlement day. Funding firmed a little: DR001 rose 1.18 bp to 1.2739%, DR007 2.57 bp to 1.3977%, overnight Shibor 1.2 bp to 1.2740% and 7-day Shibor 2.3 bp to 1.3960%, with 1-year state-bank NCDs about 1.42% (flat); Wang Qing puts the November DR001 mean at 1.29% against 1.39% in June to September and expects the medium-term tools to return to net injections, Ming Ming of CITIC expects funding rates to ease once the package lands, and Dong Ximiao describes the mix as the short end managing the floor and the middle managing the pace. The active 10-year CGB (26 coupon bond 16) was 1.5815% at the 16:03 report, down 0.35 bp, the 30-year 2.029% (−0.5 bp) and the 10-year future 0.06% higher at 110.115. The PBoC sold CNY 20B of 3-month bills at 1.32% and CNY 30B of 1-year bills at 1.41% in Hong Kong on 24 Nov; the fix was set 9 pips stronger at 6.7111 on 24 Nov and 23 pips stronger at 6.7088 on 25 Nov, the onshore yuan closed 5 pips weaker at 6.6648 at 16:30 with the offshore rate at 6.6647 at 18:00 and the dollar index down 0.48% at 103.814. The stance stays Easing by instrument with the LPR on hold; the MLF reduction is a quantity choice at an unchanged price, and the 7-day operation is the cross-month backstop."},"cbName":"PBoC stance","conflicts":[{"a":"October exports +35.2% y/y with integrated circuits +137.1%; January to October trade with other APEC economies +25.4% (GAC); export delivery value +18.6%; high-tech manufacturing output +17.6%; CAAM vehicle exports +60.2%; PPI +5.7%; RatingDog manufacturing 52.0, an 11th month above 50; TSF stock growth up to 7.2%; SAFE October bank FX settlement surplus $55.0B; January to October fiscal revenue +4.9% with securities stamp duty +54.1% and high-tech FDI +31.3%; Alibaba revenue +10% with AI cloud +53%; NEA October power consumption +1.6% y/y (January to October +3.7%)","b":"October industrial production 4.8% (consensus 5.3%), retail sales 0.4% (consensus 0.8%) with autos −21.4%, FAI −8.1% year to date with property −21.6%, infrastructure −5.1% and manufacturing −2.9%, services production index 4.6%; NBS manufacturing PMI 49.3 with new orders 49.4, non-manufacturing 49.7 with construction 48.0; CPI 0.7% with food −2.9%; new yuan loans −CNY 100B with household loans −CNY 430B; consumer confidence 89.0; NetEase games revenue −1.7%, the first fall since 2024, and Youdao −12.3%; Baidu online marketing −22%; Xiaomi Q3 revenue −5.2%, its first decline","read":"The exporter, upstream and AI-capex economy is growing at double-digit rates while the domestic demand economy is flat to contracting and platform profits are being spent on chips; the framework reads leading over coincident, and both are below 50 or decelerating. Regime Slowdown.","trigger":"27 Nov October industrial profits; 30 Nov NBS PMIs (new orders above 50 reopens Recovery; manufacturing below 49 raises Contraction); 8 Dec trade; mid-December activity data"},{"a":"PPI +5.7% y/y and purchase prices +7.9% with coal mining +36.6% and oil and gas extraction +35.0%; CICC: Qinhuangdao thermal coal CNY 1,019 a tonne, +24% y/y; US October PPI 6.5% y/y with FedWatch at about 94% for a December hike and JPMorgan expecting three hikes; TrendForce: DRAM contract prices +10% to 15% in Q4; Alibaba: 2027 and 2028 the tightest compute years","b":"PPI m/m slowed to 0.7% from 1.2%; CPI 0.7% with food −2.9%, core 0.8% and services 0.7%; retail sales 0.4% and consumer confidence 89.0; LME copper $11,826 on 24 Nov after a 5.31% fall to an 11-month low, 16% below 9 Nov, with stocks rising; tin −7.25%, aluminium −3.08%; COMEX gold −2.78% to $3,550; WTI $82.05 and Brent $91.40 after rises of 2.4% and 2.3% on 24 Nov; iron ore $90.67; the active 10-year CGB at 1.5815% and the LPR held with no cut expected before 2027; the US 10-year 4.9038%","read":"The producer-price pulse is cost-push from coal, oil and chips, not domestic demand; the metals break of 17 to 24 Nov and Goldman's memory-price cut say the cost side is rolling over while oil is back above $80 on Hormuz and the consumer side has not moved; the bond market prices neither inflation nor a cut. Inflation score stays at 48.","trigger":"9 Dec CPI and PPI (whether the m/m slowdown and the oil and metals fall show in the y/y); the 9 Dec FOMC"},{"a":"Truce extended to 10 Jan 2027; Xi and Trump agreed on 19 Nov to draft an action plan on a constructive relationship of strategic stability and are reported to plan a G20 meeting in Miami on 14 to 15 Dec; MOFCOM on 24 Nov extended the suspension of the gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard-material export ban to the US from 28 Nov to 27 Jan 2027; Trump on 20 Nov called the summit 'very successful' and said the Board of Trade's agriculture working group is due before year-end; MOFCOM opened FTA 4.0 talks with Singapore; the October US surplus about $33B with exports to the US +32.9%","b":"No new tariff rates, rare-earth quotas or purchase commitments in the official texts; US media report the administration preparing to raise tariffs on dozens of countries and USTR Greer an industrial-subsidy investigation covering the EU; Trump wants 'only older chips' to go to China; the BIS remote-access rule of 16 Nov stands and Commerce is reported to have added Alibaba's Apex Enterprise Solutions to the entity list; Nvidia's Q4 guide excludes China and its shares fell 5.86% on 24 Nov with the semiconductor index −7.88%; the EU moves to hybrid-vehicle safeguards from 1 Dec; Alibaba says models will train on domestic chips","read":"Beijing extended the minerals pause two months past the truce date while Washington's chip and tariff channels and Brussels' auto channel kept tightening; the trade channel stays open under a truce dated to 10 Jan 2027 and the only reciprocal step reported is a planned December meeting.","trigger":"Any US response to the 24 Nov suspension; the reported tariff increases and the USTR subsidy investigation; the 1 Dec EU safeguard; the agriculture working group meeting; 8 Dec trade data; 14 to 15 Dec G20 Miami; 10 Jan 2027 truce expiry"},{"a":"Home prices −2.4% y/y in October after −2.8%, the smallest fall since November 2025, and −0.1% m/m; Shanghai +2.7% with tier-one resale prices up an eighth month; second-hand transactions +11.4% year to date; new mortgage rates about 3.1%; unemployment 5.1%; the 5-year LPR at 3.50% with Dong Ximiao seeing a possible cut around year-end","b":"Property investment −21.6% year to date (Western Securities: October alone −33.2%), new-home sales −13.7% by area and −14.3% by value, cement output −1.3%; household loans −CNY 430B in October with medium and long-term loans falling; CAAM domestic vehicle sales −26.6%; construction PMI 48.0 with construction new orders 40.0; iron ore $90.67 and LME copper $11,826; 25 Huafa 04 fell 31% on 20 Nov after 22 Huafa 03 fell 25% on 19 Nov; 23 Huazong 03 −26.41%; R&F's H16 R&F 5 holders approved a grace period while the restructuring proposal failed; 22 Huafa Industrial MTN001A fell 43.31% on 23 Nov; Vanke's 22 Vanke MTN004 (CNY 1.199B, due 15 Dec) goes to an extension vote on 8 Dec; NAFMII censured Tianjin Real Estate Group; Jinke, Risesun and CFLD traded below CNY 1","read":"Prices are stabilising in the tier-one resale market while volumes, investment and developer credit keep falling and the Huafa curve is still repricing bond by bond; the property cycle is the drag on local finances, household wealth and commodity demand. Signal warn on prices, bad on investment.","trigger":"Mid-December 70-city prices and property investment; Vanke's 8 Dec MTN004 vote (ballots by 10 Dec, principal due 15 Dec); Huafa extension outcomes; R&F's next step after the failed proposal; the December Politburo meeting and Central Economic Work Conference"},{"a":"Equity support from the regulator and money at the anchor: the margin-financing minimum falls to 80% from 30 Nov (Xinhua: close to CNY 400B theoretical), draft ChiNext market-making, more than CNY 4.6B of fee relief, brokers allowed to ease forced selling, Shenzhen regulators pushing 40 listed companies toward buybacks; the PBoC injected a net CNY 16.5B on 24 Nov at 1.25% with DR001 1.2739% and set a CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo for 25 Nov to cover month-end; the active 10-year CGB 1.5815%; TSF stock growth up to 7.2%; CPI 0.7% leaves room; two-exchange turnover up 6.6% to CNY 1,655.1B on 24 Nov with main funds a net CNY 5.99B in; southbound buying of HK$6.20B","b":"The CSI 300 rose 0.14% to 3,963.82 in a session that opened strong and faded, with the ChiNext giving up a 4% gain, 3,498 stocks down against 1,952 up and metals and oil sold; the Hang Seng fell a sixth day to an 18-month low with the tech index at a two-year low; the 25 Nov MLF is CNY 800B against CNY 1T maturing and the medium-term tools net a CNY 500B drain in November; the LPR held at 3.00% for an 18th month with Wang Qing putting the next cut in 2027; the margin balance fell CNY 8.99B to CNY 2,134.81B on 23 Nov; the semiconductor index fell 7.88% in New York and copper 5.31%; a Politburo member was placed under investigation; Dongfang Jincheng expects no growth package before year-end","read":"The policy response to the sell-off is leverage and cost on the equity side and the anchor plus a cross-month backstop on the money side, while the MLF is trimmed, the LPR channel stays blocked by bank margins and fiscal stays revenue-only; the rebound it bought lasted one broad day and one narrow one, and Hong Kong, which has no margin-ratio lever, keeps making lows. PBoC stance Easing, policy score 60.","trigger":"25 Nov: whether DR001 holds within 5 bp of 1.25% through the CNY 800B MLF, the CNY 500B 7-day operation, CNY 596B of maturities and reserve settlement; 27 Nov industrial profits; the 30 Nov margin-ratio cut and whether margin balances turn up; the 9 Dec FOMC; the December Politburo meeting and Central Economic Work Conference; 21 Dec LPR"}],"drivers":[{"date":"2026-11-24","impact":"A second small large-cap gain on fading breadth: the package rally of 23 Nov did not carry into a second day in the small caps, and the index sits on its October low with the signal bad.","src":"FX168 flash; China Securities Journal via ce.cn; agudashi; Tencent daily kline; 10jqka financial breakfast","tag":"Markets","title":"24 Nov close: CSI 300 +0.14% to 3,963.82 (+5.53), 5.68 points above the 23 Oct low and 6.0% below the 4,217.68 reversal line; Shanghai Composite +0.27% to 3,548.37 (open 3,567.84, high 3,585.22, low 3,539.01); Shenzhen Component −0.29% to 10,423.60; ChiNext −0.05% to 2,278.99 after opening at 2,368.70 and rising more than 4%; STAR 50 +1.81% to 1,250.09; SSE 50 +0.45%; CSI 1000 −0.23%; BSE 50 −0.22%. Two-exchange turnover CNY 1,655.1B (+CNY 102.2B, +6.58%); 1,952 up, 3,498 down, 64 limit-ups, 4 limit-downs. Defence +1.52%, electronics +1.51% (physical AI, Industrial Fulian +6.97% on a CNY 13.29B dividend); nonferrous metals −2.53%, oil −1.94% (Zijin −4.33%); Innolight and Eoptolink opened 10% and 8% higher and closed lower. Main funds +CNY 5.99B; margin balance CNY 2,134.81B on 23 Nov (−CNY 8.99B).","url":"https://www.fx168news.com/express/fastnews/1474719"},{"date":"2026-11-24","impact":"Hong Kong has no margin-ratio lever and is pricing the AI-capex and consumer slowdown directly; southbound money returned but the index made a new low.","src":"Xinhua; FX168; Tencent hkHSI kline; VOCO; Tiger Brokers; Titanium Media via Sohu; China Securities Journal via 21st Century Business Herald","tag":"Markets","title":"Hong Kong 24 Nov: Hang Seng −0.73% to 22,219.65 (−164.09; open 22,627.29, high 22,647.50, low 22,183.16) on HK$212.63B, a sixth fall and the lowest close in more than 18 months; HSCEI −1.0% to 7,452.56; tech index −1.17% to 3,466.87, a two-year low below 3,500; red chips −1.22%. Xiaomi −3.71% before Q3 revenue of CNY 107.24B (−5.2%), Meituan −3.31%, Zhipu −6.23%, Alibaba −1.02%, Tencent −0.7%, PetroChina −3.82%, China Hongqiao −4.9%; Lenovo +3.70%, XPeng +2.86%, Hua Hong +1.55%; Public Financial Holdings +76% on Public Bank's HK$2.50 privatisation. Southbound net buying HK$6.20B (Xiaomi HK$1.09B, Hua Hong HK$0.94B; CNOOC −HK$0.52B), November to date +HK$21.70B.","url":"http://www.xinhuanet.com/20261124/860759fa1b254325a2af738ecd1108d6/c.html"},{"date":"2026-11-24","impact":"Quantity trimmed at an unchanged price with a cross-month backstop; the LPR channel stays blocked and the stance stays Easing by instrument.","src":"cnfin money market daily; 10jqka fixed-income daily; Sohu via Cailianshe; 10jqka via Securities Times; Sing Tao; FX168; China News Service","tag":"Policy","title":"PBoC on 24 Nov: CNY 516B overnight reverse repo at 1.25% against CNY 499.5B maturing, a CNY 16.5B net injection; Hong Kong bills sold at 1.32% (3-month, CNY 20B) and 1.41% (1-year, CNY 30B). After the close: CNY 800B 1-year MLF on 25 Nov against CNY 1T maturing (−CNY 200B; with the CNY 300B outright-repo cut the medium-term tools net −CNY 500B in November) plus a CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo, the first 7-day operation since the overnight rate became the anchor; CNY 516B of overnight repos and CNY 80B of treasury deposits also mature on 25 Nov. DR001 1.2739% (+1.18 bp), DR007 1.3977% (+2.57 bp), overnight Shibor 1.2740%; active 10-year CGB 1.5815% (−0.35 bp) at 16:03, 30-year 2.029%; fix 6.7111 (+9 pips), onshore close 6.6648 (−5 pips), offshore 6.6647; 25 Nov fix 6.7088 (+23 pips). Wang Qing: November DR001 mean 1.29% against 1.39% in June to September, medium-term tools to return to net injections; Ming Ming: funding to ease back; Dong Ximiao: short end manages the floor, middle manages the pace.","url":"https://www.sohu.com/a/1105877869_222256"},{"date":"2026-11-24","impact":"The critical-minerals channel stays open two months past the 10 Jan truce date while the chip and tariff channels tighten from Washington and the auto channel from Brussels.","src":"SMM; The News; Eastmoney financial breakfast; 21st Century Business Herald morning brief; Fastmarkets; VOCO","tag":"Trade","title":"MOFCOM suspends the second paragraph of Announcement 2024 No. 46 (no export licences for gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard-material dual-use items to the US; stricter end-use review for graphite) from 28 Nov 2026 to 27 Jan 2027, extending the pause agreed in November 2025 that was due to lapse this week; the rare-earth pause is separately dated to 10 Jan 2027; no US step reported in return. Same day: the European Commission issued a preliminary finding in its hybrid-vehicle safeguard case with temporary measures from 1 Dec, and MOFCOM reserved WTO dispute settlement and trade compensation; unnamed sources told US media the administration is preparing to raise tariffs on dozens of countries and that USTR Greer may announce an industrial-subsidy investigation covering the EU as soon as this week; VOCO reports Commerce added Alibaba's Singapore unit Apex Enterprise Solutions and six entities to the entity list, with Alibaba saying Apex never transferred controlled chips; Xi and Trump are reported to plan a meeting at the G20 in Miami on 14 to 15 Dec.","url":"https://news.metal.com/newscontent/3C2IIURHWKUKCCSNKNPEEUTFZL4A7G4AKEH4FWQ-china-suspends-export-controls-on-certain-dual-use-items-to-us-from-nov-28-2026-to-jan-27-2027"},{"date":"2026-11-24","impact":"A sitting Politburo member and the leader of the largest financial centre removed two weeks before the December Politburo meeting and the Central Economic Work Conference; the market read is governance risk rather than policy change.","src":"Xinhua; China News Service; People's Daily; 21st Century Business Herald morning brief; The Paper (SASAC notice)","tag":"Politics","title":"Xinhua: Chen Jining, Politburo member and Shanghai party secretary, is under CCDI and National Supervisory Commission investigation for suspected serious violations of discipline and law. SASAC also announced leadership changes at 14 central SOEs including CNBM, China Resources Recycling and OCT.","url":"https://www.news.cn/20261124/c9efb02bd8be4a4cbbbee2102cfbc657/c.html"},{"date":"2026-11-24","impact":"The developer curve is still repricing bond by bond with Vanke's first public extension vote now dated; the property drag on local finances and commodity demand is unchanged.","src":"Vanke HK filing via Sina; Jiemian via Sina; 21st Century Business Herald bond brief; China Securities Journal via Sina","tag":"Property","title":"Vanke's 22 Vanke MTN004 (CNY 1.199B outstanding, principal due 15 Dec, Shanghai Pudong Development Bank as agent) goes to a second holder meeting on 8 Dec to vote on extension terms (record date 7 Dec, votes by 17:00 on 10 Dec); R&F's H16 R&F 5 holders approved a grace period while the restructuring proposal failed; NAFMII disciplined five issuers including Tianjin Real Estate Group (public censure, business suspended) and China Minsheng Investment and barred Guanghui Auto for two years; 22 Huafa Industrial MTN001A fell 43.31% on 23 Nov; Beijing's 15th five-year urban renewal plan targets CNY 300B a year of investment by 2030.","url":"https://k.sina.cn/article_5182171545_134e1a99902002ls32.html"},{"date":"2026-11-24","impact":"The AI-hardware reversal and the copper break hit the two channels that had been carrying China's exporter economy and its demand gauge.","src":"Eastmoney financial breakfast; 10jqka via Dahe Caili Fang; 21st Century Business Herald; Xinhua Finance via Eastmoney; Fastmarkets; Westmetall; Trading Economics","tag":"Markets","title":"New York 24 Nov: Philadelphia semiconductor index −7.88% with all 30 members lower, Nvidia −5.86% to $155.38 after Monday's +31.48%, Micron −11.01%, SanDisk −11.13%, AMD −8.86%, Intel −8.15%, TSMC −3.83% after Goldman cut 2028 DRAM and NAND price forecasts by about 20%; Nasdaq −1.48% to 23,733.54, S&P 500 −0.50% to 7,201.09, Dow +0.85% to 50,018.70; Golden Dragon +0.12%, Alibaba ADR −1.37%. Conference Board confidence 103.3 (+11.4; 92.5 expected); US 10-year 4.9038% (−4.0 bp), 2-year 4.6705%, dollar index 103.814 (−0.48%), USD/JPY 159.21; eight of twelve reserve banks asked for a discount-rate hike. Nikkei +3.91% to 58,644.63, Kospi +6.32% to 5,006.03, DAX −1.26%. LME copper −5.31% to $11,826 (Fastmarkets: 3-month $11,858.50, an 11-month low; Westmetall 23 Nov settlement $12,165), tin −7.25% to $39,539, aluminium −3.08% to $2,769, cobalt +14.96% to $38,540; WTI +2.35% to $82.05, Brent +2.27% to $91.40 as the IRGC said Hormuz stays closed; COMEX gold −2.78% to $3,550.00, silver −6.10%; iron ore flat at $90.67.","url":"https://m.21jingji.com/article/20261125/herald/1f8fd69ef8a60f80e0372fa860e459bf.html"},{"date":"2026-11-24","impact":"Xiaomi's 5.2% revenue decline confirms the consumer-electronics and EV price pressure the October retail data showed; dividends and buybacks are the policy-encouraged offset.","src":"21st Century Business Herald morning brief; 10jqka financial breakfast; Eastmoney financial breakfast; China Securities Journal via Sina; NewsNow close recap","tag":"Earnings","title":"Xiaomi Q3: revenue CNY 107.24B, −5.2% y/y (smartphones CNY 45.6B, +8.2% q/q; EVs and AI CNY 23.9B), with buybacks of about HK$13.1B year to date; shares −3.71% ahead of the release. Bilibili Q3 revenue CNY 8.32B (+8%). Industrial Fulian declared a CNY 0.67 a share interim dividend (CNY 13.29B, 32.9% of nine-month profit); Victory Giant CNY 1.00 a share. Qinghai Salt Lake proposed a CNY 1.5B to 2B buyback for cancellation, Innolight CNY 2B to 4B, Wanhua's chairman CNY 300M to 500M; Shenzhen regulators met 40 listed companies to push buybacks and insider purchases. Dayi Intelligent goes to ST on 26 Nov after a CSRC penalty notice for false 2021 and 2022 reports. Tianqi Lithium to buy 76.53% of Runfeng Mining and related assets for about CNY 6.87B.","url":"https://m.21jingji.com/article/20261125/herald/5fa034e644720c87705c3b01bdc4b955.html"},{"date":"2026-11-23","impact":"The package produced a broad small-cap rebound with the large-cap index flat on its October low and Friday's defensive leaders sold; a bounce inside Risk-off, not a reversal.","src":"Jinrongjie via Sohu; Eastmoney; FX168; Gelonghui via Sina; 21st Century Business Herald","tag":"Markets","title":"23 Nov close: CSI 300 +0.09% to 3,958.29 (+3.72), 0.15 points above the 23 Oct low of 3,958.14 it broke on Friday; Shanghai Composite +0.15% to 3,538.95, Shenzhen Component +1.93% to 10,454.37, ChiNext +3.08% to 2,280.20 after a 1% intraday fall, CSI 500 +2.05%, CSI 1000 +2.90% to 5,812.32, National 2000 +3.34%, BSE 50 +4.67% to 795.38, STAR 50 −0.26% to 1,227.89. Two-exchange turnover CNY 1.55T (+CNY 130.7B), more than 4,600 up, 151 limit-ups; robotics, film and AI short drama, medical services, precious metals, PCB and CPO and pork led, insurers (China Pacific, Ping An −3%), nuclear, oil and gas, coal, autos and state banks fell. ETFs +CNY 7.41B net (stock ETFs +CNY 12.82B; Southern CSI 1000 ETF +CNY 3.46B), ETF margin balance +CNY 1.71B to CNY 122.02B, convertible index +2.15%; 18 new active ETFs traded CNY 8.01B with 13 of 18 down; more than 30 buybacks announced including Innolight (CNY 2B to 4B) and Moore Threads (CNY 0.5B to 1B).","url":"https://www.sohu.com/a/1105257248_114984"},{"date":"2026-11-23","impact":"Hong Kong did not follow the mainland bounce and the southbound bid that held it last week reversed through the index ETFs; the auto margin story is a new drag on the EV names.","src":"Xinhua via Sina; Sina Finance; China Fund News via 21st Century Business Herald; 10jqka citing Securities Times","tag":"Markets","title":"Hong Kong 23 Nov: Hang Seng −0.12% to 22,383.74 (−27.06) on HK$253.09B, a fifth fall; HSCEI −0.35% to 7,527.98; tech index −0.09% to 3,508. Leapmotor −12.99% on a 10.9% Q3 gross margin (revenue CNY 31.70B, +63.0%), XPeng −6.3%, NIO −3.9% as CAAM reviews supplier payment terms at 17 carmakers; Lenovo +7.58% to HK$17.59, Lingbao Gold +10%, WuXi Biologics +4%, Innolight +4.80%, Zhipu +1.86% on GLM-5.4; Tencent flat at HK$344, Alibaba −0.36%, HKEX −1.57%, CCB −1.62%, CNOOC −1.94%. Southbound net sale HK$9.63B on HK$95.57B, the first after four days of buying: Tracker Fund −HK$7.93B across the two channels, Southern Hang Seng Tech ETF −HK$1.97B, Hang Seng China Enterprises ETF −HK$1.67B; Alibaba +HK$1.42B, Meituan +HK$892M, CCB +HK$397M bought.","url":"https://k.sina.cn/article_2810373291_a782e4ab0200318bz.html"},{"date":"2026-11-23","impact":"The price of money stayed at the anchor with the quantity restored ahead of the MLF maturity and month-end; the bond market ignored the equity package and the yuan firmed against a stronger dollar.","src":"cnfin; 10jqka; Eastmoney; FX168; Jiemian; stnn; China News Service; MoneyDJ via Yahoo","tag":"Policy","title":"PBoC on 23 Nov: CNY 499.5B overnight reverse repo at 1.25% against CNY 379.5B maturing, a CNY 120B net injection after Friday's CNY 688B drain, with CNY 1T of MLF maturing this week. DR001 −0.1 bp to 1.2621%, R001 +1.0 bp to 1.3479%, DR007 +0.8 bp to 1.3720%, R007 +1.1 bp to 1.4074%, overnight Shibor +0.08 bp to 1.2620%, 7-day Shibor +1.1 bp to 1.3730%, 1-year state-bank NCDs about 1.42%; the market balanced and looser into the close. Active 10-year CGB 1.5825% (+0.25 bp; Eastmoney 1.581%), 30-year 2.061% (+1.4 bp), 10-year CDB 1.674%, TL future −0.25% to 117.91, T −0.03% to 110.045. Fix 6.7120 (+11 pips stronger), onshore close 6.6643 (+92 pips), offshore 6.6668 at 18:00; 24 Nov fix 6.7111 (+9 pips). CNY 50B Hong Kong bill tender on 24 Nov (CNY 20B 3-month, CNY 30B 1-year).","url":"https://www.cnfin.com/hb-lb/detail/20261123/4499247_1.html"},{"date":"2026-11-23","impact":"The AI unwind that spread to Hong Kong, Tokyo and Seoul last week reversed on a governance headline; a relief for the Hang Seng tech names and the chip channel, not a change in the export-control facts.","src":"Sina Finance US close reports (24 Nov 05:18 and 06:12); Sohu international morning brief (24 Nov); Eastmoney financial breakfast (24 Nov)","tag":"Markets","title":"New York 23 Nov: S&P 500 +4.73% to 7,237.17, ending a seven-day fall with its largest gain since April 2025; Dow +1,447.98 (+3.01%) to 49,595.31; Nasdaq +6.51% to 24,089.56; Nasdaq 100 +6.9%; Russell 2000 +3.4%. Nvidia +31.48%, its largest gain since May 2003 and about $952B of value added in a day, after its board unanimously reinstated Jensen Huang as president, CEO and director, saying it had consulted senior US officials and found no national-security risk, with Trump saying he persuaded the board; Micron +19%, CoreWeave +22%, Tesla +11%, Magnificent Seven +7.5%, Anthropic −1.43%. US 10-year 4.9218% (−2.2 bp), dollar index 104.318 (+0.49%), WTI $80.17 (−3.88%), Brent $89.37 (−3.46%), COMEX gold $3,635.20 (+3.41%), LME copper $12,490 (+$330). NY Fed's Williams: the Fed still has work to do on inflation; flash November PMIs 54.5 manufacturing, 54.7 services. DAX +2.15%; Nikkei opened +1.02% and the Kospi +3.64% on 24 Nov. Amazon to buy Decart for about $7.5B; CrowdStrike to buy Zscaler for about $43.9B; DRC suspends cobalt exports from 30 Nov.","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/stock/usstock/c/2026-11-24/doc-inizupfs0253751.shtml"},{"date":"2026-11-22","impact":"Leverage, liquidity and cost support for equities after the broad market's worst week of the year; it addresses the sell-off's mechanics, not the demand data behind the Slowdown regime.","src":"Xinhua (22 Nov); Caiwen via Sohu (22 Nov); Eastmoney financial breakfast (24 Nov); FX168 (23 Nov: CITIC, China Merchants)","tag":"Policy","title":"Market-stabilisation package (Saturday 22 Nov): with CSRC approval the Shanghai, Shenzhen and Beijing exchanges cut the minimum margin-financing ratio from 100% to 80% from 30 Nov (1.25x cap in place of 1x; the ratio was cut to 80% in August 2023 and raised to 100% in January 2026; Xinhua cites an estimate of close to CNY 400B of theoretical incremental money); the Shenzhen exchange published draft ChiNext market-making rules for comment; the Shanghai and Shenzhen exchanges added CNY 1.368B and CNY 1.39B of fee relief for 2026 totals above CNY 2.4B and CNY 2.2B (more than CNY 4.6B combined), waiving trading-unit and listing fees and extending bond-handling waivers to 2028; CSDC waives issuer and settlement fees on green, technology and private-enterprise bonds from 1 Jan 2027 to end-2028. Regulators separately told brokers they may adjust maintenance ratios and margin-call liquidation with client consent in volatile periods and avoid concentrated forced selling.","url":"https://www.news.cn/fortune/20261122/3ee9d44d8c4545dfb106561707cd6c2f/c.html"},{"date":"2026-11-20","impact":"The October low is gone on rising turnover with nine in ten stocks down; the posture stays Risk-off and the range runs toward 3,900. Markets score 24 (from 27).","src":"urasr (禾略) review; Sina Finance close report; 21st Century Business Herald; Sina 情绪罗盘; 10jqka financial breakfast (21 Nov); Sina Tech weekly summary","tag":"Markets","title":"20 Nov close: CSI 300 −0.76% to 3,954.57 (−30.27), the first close below the 23 Oct low of 3,958.14 after three intraday breaks; Shanghai Composite −1.22% to 3,533.79 (open 3,527.30, high 3,538.27, low 3,500.83, a 52-week low); Shenzhen Component −3.09% to 10,256.39, ChiNext −3.54% to 2,212.13, STAR 50 −3.12% to 1,231.09, CSI 500 −3.93%, CSI 1000 −4.89% to 5,648.63, CSI 2000 −5.36%, BSE 50 −4.85% to 759.90, Wind micro-cap −6.14% (seventh fall); SSE 50 +0.45%. Two-exchange turnover about CNY 1.42T (+CNY 117B; 10jqka CNY 1,431.1B), 297 up, 4,897 down, 30 limit-ups, 68 limit-downs. Banks and insurers the only sectors up (ICBC +3%, PetroChina +4%, CCB, BoC, BoCom, CITIC Bank and Yangtze Power record highs); semiconductors −6.85%, lithography −7.79%, memory −6.61%, military electronics −6.88%, 阿石创 −16%. Huaxia SSE 50 ETF turnover above CNY 22B and Harvest CSI 300 ETF above CNY 23.4B, both records. Week: Shanghai Composite −2.77%, Shenzhen Component −6.49%, ChiNext −8.82%, STAR 50 −3.80%, BSE 50 −13.29%, SSE 50 +0.39%; 427 up, 5,135 down; average daily turnover CNY 1,417.6B (−CNY 245.1B).","url":"https://www.urasr.com/caixun/2026-11-20.html"},{"date":"2026-11-20","impact":"Words on AI guardrails and older chips, no terms on trade; the technology channel stays closed from both sides and the trade channel runs on a truce dated to 10 Jan 2027. Neutral for the regime, Risk-off unchanged.","src":"NPR via UALR Public Radio and GPB (press conference); China Briefing (summit tally); 10jqka financial breakfast (21 Nov: Huang remark, MOFCOM-Singapore)","tag":"Geopolitics","title":"Trump's White House press conference on the trip (20 Nov): the Shenzhen meeting 'very successful' and the trilateral historic; 'President Xi and I agree that we're going to do some joint guardrails' on AI; 'we're not going to allow our companies to build data centers outside of our country' and a tax on those that do; on chips, 'we want only older chips, and we don't mind if none go, but only older'; wants Jensen Huang to apologise and return to Nvidia; oil prices 'closely tied to how things are going in Iran' and 'a real deal, not a fake deal'. No statement reported on tariffs, rare earths, farm purchases, the Board of Trade, Taiwan or Ukraine (NPR, GPB). China Briefing's tally of Shenzhen: an action plan with no timeline or content, no new tariff rates, the truce and the suspensions (China's 24% tariff, rare-earth controls, port fees; the US Affiliates Rule) running to 10 Jan 2027, the Board of Trade's 13 Nov meeting without agreement and an agriculture working group due before year-end. MOFCOM and Singapore signed an MoU on 20 Nov to launch negotiations on a 4.0 upgrade of the China-Singapore FTA (government procurement, digital trade).","url":"https://www.ualrpublicradio.org/npr-news/2026-11-20/trump-holds-press-conference-after-meeting-with-xi-and-putin"},{"date":"2026-11-20","impact":"The 18th hold was fully expected and the analysts have pushed the next cut into 2027 or to year-end at the earliest; the PBoC is easing through the overnight rate and relending, not the LPR. PBoC stance Easing, policy score 60.","src":"The Paper and China News Service (LPR announcement); 21st Century Business Herald; Jiemian via Sohu (Wang Qing, Dong Ximiao); China News Service and Beijing Business Today via Sina (fixing)","tag":"Policy","title":"November LPR held: 1-year 3.00%, 5-year 3.50%, an 18th month unchanged since the 10 bp cut of May 2025. Wang Qing (Dongfang Jincheng): bank net interest margins near historic lows leave quoting banks no incentive to cut; Q3 GDP 4.5% with strong exports and high-tech manufacturing; the October miss is a normal monthly fluctuation and the 4.5% to 5.0% target is reachable; the 29 Sep structural tools (PSL −25 bp, CNY 500B more relending, first-home mortgage interest subsidy) show a preference for structural measures; a near-term LPR cut is unlikely, a broad 10 to 20 bp cut likely in 2027. Dong Ximiao (Zhaolian): domestic demand is weak and household medium and long-term loans fell in October; a small LPR fall is possible after the December Central Economic Work Conference, around year-end, depending on data. October new corporate loan rate about 2.9% (−0.2 pt y/y), new mortgages about 3.1%; the Q3 report pushes multiple pricing benchmarks including DR001-linked floating loans. Fix 6.7131 (−3 pips); onshore yuan about 6.676 in the morning after a 6.6910 night close.","url":"https://www.chinanews.com.cn/cj/2026/11-20/10735037.shtml"}],"headline":"The CSI 300 rose 0.14% to 3,963.82 on 24 Nov, 5.68 points above its October low, in a session that opened strong and faded: the ChiNext gave up a 4% intraday gain to close 0.05% lower, 3,498 stocks fell against 1,952 up on two-exchange turnover up 6.6% to CNY 1,655.1B, and the Hang Seng fell a sixth day, 0.73% to 22,219.65, its lowest close in more than 18 months, with the tech index at 3,466.87 and Xiaomi −3.71% before reporting Q3 revenue down 5.2%; the PBoC injected a net CNY 16.5B overnight and announced a CNY 800B MLF against CNY 1T maturing plus a CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo for 25 Nov, the 10-year CGB was 1.5815%, the yuan closed at 6.6648 with the fix at 6.7088 on 25 Nov, MOFCOM extended the suspension of its gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard-material export ban to the US from 28 Nov to 27 Jan 2027, Shanghai party secretary Chen Jining was placed under CCDI investigation, LME copper fell 5.31% to $11,826 and the Philadelphia semiconductor index fell 7.88% with Nvidia −5.86%; the regime stays Slowdown, the posture Risk-off and the PBoC stance Easing.","marketClose":"Tue 24 Nov 2026 (mainland and Hong Kong)","notes":["Mainland closes are for Tuesday 24 Nov: the CSI 300 (3,963.82, +5.53, +0.14%), Shanghai Composite (3,548.37, +9.42, +0.27%), Shenzhen Component (10,423.60, −0.29%), ChiNext (2,278.99, −0.05%) and STAR 50 (1,250.09, +1.81%) are the FX168 flash, matching Jin10 via NewsNow and the China Securities Journal % changes; the Shanghai open, high and low are Tencent's daily kline (the sh000300 kline was stale at 20 Nov and was not used). No page gave the CSI 300 open, high or low.","Two-exchange turnover for 24 Nov is CNY 1,655.086B (+CNY 102.206B, +6.58%; Shanghai CNY 771.861B, Shenzhen CNY 883.225B) from agudashi and Sina; the 10jqka breakfast prints a whole-market CNY 1,667.8B (+CNY 103.8B) and the China Securities Journal 'about CNY 1.67T, +CNY 103.8B'. Breadth (1,952 up, 3,498 down, 64 limit-ups, 4 limit-downs) is the China Securities Journal; agudashi's 5,580-stock sample including Beijing gives 1,951 up. The margin balance (CNY 2,134.807B, −CNY 8.985B) and ETF flows (net CNY 7.414B) are for 23 Nov from the 10jqka breakfast; no 24 Nov margin or ETF flow figure was published by the pages opened.","Hong Kong closes for 24 Nov are Xinhua (Hang Seng 22,219.65, −164.09; HSCEI 7,452.56; tech index 3,466.87; main-board turnover HK$212.633B), matching FX168, 21st Century Business Herald and Tiger; the open, high and low are Tencent's hkHSI kline (22,627.29 / 22,647.50 / 22,183.16), consistent with VOCO's rounded figures. Southbound net buying of HK$6.204B is Titanium Media via Sohu and VOCO (21st Century Business Herald: 'more than HK$6.2B'); Securities Times headlines HK$8.571B for the same day on a page that could not be opened (robots), so the lower figure is used and the discrepancy is unresolved. No Shanghai and Shenzhen channel split was published by the pages opened.","The 10-year CGB point for 24 Nov is 1.5815% (−0.35 bp) for the active bond 26 coupon bond 16 in the 10jqka fixed-income daily stamped 16:03, a late-session level rather than a confirmed close; two Sohu commentaries at 14:00 put the intraday move at 'nearly 1 bp lower' and '+0.5 bp' respectively and are not used. The 30-year quoted on 24 Nov (26 ultra-long special 06, 2.029%) is a different bond from the 04 issue quoted on 23 Nov (2.061%), so the two days' 30-year figures are not comparable.","PBoC operations for 24 Nov (CNY 516B overnight at 1.25% against CNY 499.5B maturing, CNY 16.5B net injection) and the funding rates are the cnfin money market daily and the 10jqka fixed-income daily; R001 and R007 were not printed. The 25 Nov announcement (CNY 800B MLF, CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo) is the PBoC via Cailianshe on Sohu, Securities Times on 10jqka and Sing Tao; the pages give no 7-day rate (the standing rate is 1.40%) and the MLF has had no single rate since 2025. The CNY 300B outright-repo reduction and CNY 500B medium-term net drain for November are Cailianshe's and Securities Times' arithmetic; the week's overnight maturities of CNY 379.5B in the Cailianshe piece differ from the CNY 516B maturing on 25 Nov in the Eastmoney breakfast, which is used. The results of the 25 Nov operations had not been published at this refresh.","USD/CNY for 24 Nov is the 16:30 onshore close of 6.6648 (FX168, '5 pips lower'; Eastmoney breakfast), the offshore 6.6647 at 18:00 (+21 pips) and the swap points are the Eastmoney breakfast; the 24 Nov fix of 6.7111 (+9 pips) is 10jqka and the 25 Nov fix of 6.7088 is China News Service, MoneyDJ and SMM (MoneyDJ: 23 pips stronger versus 6.7111; China News Service's wording 'raised 23 pips' conflicts with the direction of the level and MoneyDJ's reading is used). The dollar index (103.814, −0.48%) and US Treasury closes (10-year 4.9038%, 2-year 4.6705%) are the Eastmoney breakfast; Xinhua Finance's intraday table prints 4.928% for the 10-year and is not used.","Copper: Westmetall's LME table now ends at 23 Nov ($12,165 cash, $12,170 3-month, 330,975 t), replacing the $12,490 Eastmoney evening close used for 23 Nov at the last refresh; the 24 Nov row and the November history pair use the Eastmoney breakfast's LME close of $11,826 (−$664, −5.31%) because no 24 Nov settlement was posted, with Fastmarkets' 15:45 3-month print of $11,858.50 (−5.05%) as the cross-check; the two bases differ by up to about $300 and the point will be replaced by the settlement when posted. Iron ore is Trading Economics' $90.67 for 24 Nov, flat on the day, with the page updated 25 Nov.","US and overseas figures for Tuesday 24 Nov are the 21st Century Business Herald and 10jqka (via Dahe Caili Fang) close reports (Dow 50,018.70, +0.85%; S&P 500 7,201.09, −0.50%; Nasdaq 23,733.54, −1.48%; semiconductor index −7.88%; Nvidia $155.38, −5.86%; WTI January $82.05 settlement; Brent $91.40; COMEX gold $3,550.00; DAX 25,017.81) and the Eastmoney breakfast and Xinhua Finance (Treasuries, dollar index, Nikkei 58,644.63, Kospi 5,006.03, euro, yen); Xinhua Finance's oil quotes ($81.69 and $88.57) are intraday and not used. The 97% December-hike probability is a Jin10 teaser and the entity-list addition of Alibaba's Apex unit is VOCO only; both are flagged as single-source.","The MOFCOM suspension is SMM citing the MOFCOM website and the Eastmoney and 10jqka breakfasts (Announcement 2024 No. 46, second paragraph, 28 Nov 2026 to 27 Jan 2027); the new announcement number, the previous window's exact dates and any US reciprocal step were not given by the pages opened (ANI and MLex pages failed). The Chen Jining investigation is Xinhua, China News Service and People's Daily (24 Nov). Xiaomi's Q3 revenue (CNY 107.24B, −5.2%) is the 10jqka and 21st Century Business Herald morning briefs; no profit figure was printed.","No Chinese activity, price, credit or trade data printed on 21 to 24 Nov. Those rows carry the figures and sources from earlier refreshes (NBS releases of 16 Nov, 9 Nov and 31 Oct; PBoC 13 Nov; GAC 10 Nov); the NEA's October power consumption (870.9 TWh, +1.6% y/y) is the China Securities Journal via Sina and is cited in the regime note only. October consumer confidence is still unpublished."],"posture":{"label":"Risk-off","note":"The CSI 300 closed at 3,963.82 on 24 Nov, up 5.53 points or 0.14%, 5.68 points above the 23 Oct low of 3,958.14 and 6.0% below the 4,217.68 reversal line, in a session that opened strong and faded: the Shanghai Composite opened at 3,567.84, reached 3,585.22 and closed at 3,548.37 (+0.27%), the ChiNext opened 3% higher at 2,368.70, rose more than 4% intraday and closed 0.05% lower at 2,278.99, its low of the day, the Shenzhen Component fell 0.29% to 10,423.60 and the STAR 50 rose 1.81% to 1,250.09 while the CSI 1000 fell 0.23% and the BSE 50 0.22%. Two-exchange turnover rose CNY 102.2B or 6.6% to CNY 1,655.1B, but breadth reversed to 1,952 up against 3,498 down with 64 limit-ups and 4 limit-downs, Innolight and Eoptolink opened 10% and 8% higher and closed lower, and nonferrous metals (−2.53%) and oil (−1.94%) led the fallers while defence (+1.52%) and electronics (+1.51%) led the gainers; main-fund flows were a net CNY 5.99B in. Hong Kong fell a sixth day: the Hang Seng opened 243 points higher at 22,627.29, reached 22,647.50 and closed 0.73% lower at 22,219.65, its lowest close in more than 18 months, on HK$212.63B (from HK$253.09B), with the tech index −1.17% at 3,466.87, a more than two-year low below 3,500, the HSCEI −1.0% at 7,452.56, Xiaomi −3.71% before reporting Q3 revenue down 5.2%, Meituan −3.31%, Zhipu −6.23%, PetroChina −3.82% and China Hongqiao −4.9%, against Lenovo +3.70% and XPeng +2.86%; southbound investors bought a net HK$6.20B (Xiaomi HK$1.09B, Hua Hong HK$0.94B; CNOOC sold HK$0.52B). Overnight the Philadelphia semiconductor index fell 7.88% with Nvidia −5.86% and Micron −11.01%, the Nasdaq fell 1.48% and LME copper fell 5.31% to $11,826 on the Eastmoney close basis, an 11-month low. A second small gain in the large caps on fading breadth, a sixth Hang Seng fall to an 18-month low and a 5% copper break keep the posture Risk-off; the reversal test is a CSI 300 close above 4,217.68 on turnover back toward CNY 2T."},"regime":{"label":"Slowdown","note":"No activity data printed on 24 Nov, so the regime still rests on the 16 Nov release: industrial production 4.8% y/y (consensus 5.3%, September 5.5%), retail sales 0.4% (consensus 0.8%) with autos −21.4%, fixed-asset investment −8.1% year to date with property −21.6%, infrastructure −5.1% and manufacturing −2.9%, the services production index 4.6%, unemployment 5.1% and the 70-city price fall narrowing to −2.4% y/y. The leading set is below 50 (NBS manufacturing PMI 49.3, new orders 49.4, non-manufacturing 49.7, construction 48.0) and consumer confidence is 89.0, so leading and coincident data agree on Slowdown. It is not Contraction because Q3 GDP is 4.5%, October exports are +35.2%, the RatingDog manufacturing PMI is 52.0, January to October fiscal revenue rose 4.9% and the NEA's October power consumption rose 1.6% y/y (870.9 TWh; January to October +3.7%). The 24 Nov news was political and external (Chen Jining under investigation, the dual-use export-control suspension extended to 27 Jan 2027, the EU's hybrid-vehicle safeguard from 1 Dec), not demand policy. The next tests are October industrial profits on 27 Nov and the 30 Nov PMIs."},"schema":1,"sections":[{"id":"leading","rows":[{"change":"−0.8","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":49.2},{"l":"Dec 25","v":50.1},{"l":"Jan 26","v":49.3},{"l":"Feb 26","v":49},{"l":"Mar 26","v":50.4},{"l":"Apr 26","v":50.3},{"l":"May 26","v":50},{"l":"Jun 26","v":50.3},{"l":"Jul 26","v":49.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":49.8},{"l":"Sep 26","v":50.1},{"l":"Oct 26","v":49.3}],"latest":"49.3","name":"NBS Manufacturing PMI","next":"30 Nov","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"50.1","read":"Fell 0.8 points to 49.3 against a 49.9 consensus, the third contraction reading in four months. Production fell 1.9 to 49.8 and new orders 1.1 to 49.4; new export orders were 48.7. Large firms held 50.2 while medium (48.4) and small (47.5) firms fell more than a point, high-tech (51.3) and equipment (50.6) stayed above 50 and consumer goods fell 1.9 to 48.8. Purchase prices fell 4.0 to 56.8 and output prices 2.3 to 51.7, still above 50 on oil; the NBS cites orders pulled forward before the holiday. The private RatingDog survey printed 52.0 two days later, so the gap between exporters and the domestic economy is 2.7 points.","ref":50,"refLabel":"50 = expansion line","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Contraction, 48-50 band","src":"NBS release (31 Oct) via The Paper, China News Service and JKN; Bloomberg consensus via China-Global South Project","trend":"down","trendWord":"Back below 50","url":"https://www.thepaper.cn/newsDetail_forward_34375155"},{"change":"−1.1","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":49.2},{"l":"Dec 25","v":50.8},{"l":"Jan 26","v":49.2},{"l":"Feb 26","v":48.6},{"l":"Mar 26","v":51.6},{"l":"Apr 26","v":50.6},{"l":"May 26","v":49.9},{"l":"Jun 26","v":51.2},{"l":"Jul 26","v":48.5},{"l":"Aug 26","v":50.6},{"l":"Sep 26","v":50.5},{"l":"Oct 26","v":49.4}],"latest":"49.4","name":"NBS Manufacturing New Orders","next":"30 Nov","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"50.5","read":"The critical demand signal fell 1.1 points to 49.4, below 50 for the first time since July (48.5). The NBS says part of October demand was released before the National Day holiday, which is consistent with the September reading of 50.5 being a subsidy and pre-holiday month. Orders (49.4) are now below production (49.8), so the inventory build of September has stopped; rail, ship, aerospace and electronics kept orders at or above 53 while textiles, non-metallic minerals and non-ferrous smelting were below 50 on both.","ref":50,"refLabel":"50 = expansion line","signal":"warn","signalWord":"First sub-50 since July","src":"NBS release (31 Oct) via The Paper and China News Service (statistician Huo Lihui)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slipped below 50","url":"https://www.chinanews.com.cn/cj/2026/10-31/10723787.shtml"},{"change":"−0.1","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":49.9},{"l":"Dec 25","v":50.1},{"l":"Jan 26","v":50.3},{"l":"Feb 26","v":52.1},{"l":"Mar 26","v":50.8},{"l":"Apr 26","v":52.2},{"l":"May 26","v":51.8},{"l":"Jun 26","v":51.7},{"l":"Jul 26","v":50.9},{"l":"Aug 26","v":51.5},{"l":"Sep 26","v":52.1},{"l":"Oct 26","v":52}],"latest":"52.0","name":"RatingDog (ex-Caixin) Manufacturing PMI","next":"1 Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"52.1","read":"Printed 52.0 on 2 Nov against a 51.6 Reuters consensus, little changed from September's 52.1 and an 11th straight month above 50, the longest run since mid-2021. Output grew at the fastest pace since April led by investment goods, new orders rose for a 17th month and new export orders for a fourth, though export growth slowed to a three-month low; output prices fell for the second time in three months, export prices fell for the first time in nearly a year and business confidence dropped to a nine-month low. The companion services PMI of 4 Nov fell to 50.8 from 51.6, a three-month low with selling prices down a second month and input costs rising at the fastest pace in five months, so the composite output index fell to 52.0 from 52.4. The survey of about 650 mostly export-oriented firms is 2.7 points above the official 49.3, the widest gap this year, so exporters are still growing while the domestic survey contracts.","ref":50,"refLabel":"50 = expansion line","signal":"good","signalWord":"11th month above 50","src":"S&P Global / RatingDog manufacturing release (2 Nov) and services release (4 Nov) via investinglive; Reuters consensus via investinglive","trend":"flat","trendWord":"Holding above 52","url":"https://www.pmi.spglobal.com/Public/Home/PressRelease/048ae0dea1f64839944545370ea523b4"},{"change":"−0.5","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":49.5},{"l":"Dec 25","v":50.2},{"l":"Jan 26","v":49.4},{"l":"Feb 26","v":49.5},{"l":"Mar 26","v":50.1},{"l":"Apr 26","v":49.4},{"l":"May 26","v":50.1},{"l":"Jun 26","v":50.2},{"l":"Jul 26","v":49},{"l":"Aug 26","v":49},{"l":"Sep 26","v":50.2},{"l":"Oct 26","v":49.7}],"latest":"49.7","name":"NBS Non-Manufacturing PMI","next":"30 Nov","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"50.2","read":"Fell 0.5 points to 49.7 after one month above 50. Services held 50.0 (−0.2) with rail, accommodation and culture rising and finance the only major category falling notably; water transport, post and internet software stayed above 55. Construction fell 2.3 to 48.0 and its new-orders index 5.7 to 40.0, the weakest part of the survey, with construction employment at 42.0 and expectations down 3.1 to 52.3. Non-manufacturing new orders were 44.4 (−2.1) and sales prices 49.5, so services firms are still cutting prices; the private RatingDog services PMI of 4 Nov agrees, at 50.8 with selling prices falling a second month.","ref":50,"refLabel":"50 = expansion line","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Construction 48.0","src":"NBS release (31 Oct) via The Paper and Xinhua; RatingDog services PMI (4 Nov) via investinglive","trend":"down","trendWord":"Back below 50","url":"https://english.news.cn/20261031/77e098a3990746ad830789748f0e712e/c.html"},{"change":"−0.5","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":89.4},{"l":"Nov 25","v":90.3},{"l":"Dec 25","v":89.5},{"l":"Jan 26","v":90.6},{"l":"Feb 26","v":91.6},{"l":"Mar 26","v":90},{"l":"Apr 26","v":89},{"l":"May 26","v":89.9},{"l":"Jun 26","v":89.4},{"l":"Jul 26","v":89.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":89.5},{"l":"Sep 26","v":89}],"latest":"89.0","name":"Consumer Confidence Index","next":"October not yet published","period":"Sep 2026","prior":"89.5","read":"Fell 0.5 points to 89.0 in September, giving back the August uptick and more than 10 points under the neutral line; the index has been inside the 89 to 92 band since 2022 and the record low was 85.5 in November 2022. The direction is down again, from 91.6 in February, and October retail sales at 0.4% y/y with autos −21.4% say the mood is reaching spending. The NBS also reported median disposable income growth of 3.9% for January to September, slower than the 4.5% mean.","ref":100,"refLabel":"100 = neutral line","signal":"bad","signalWord":"Far below 100","src":"NBS via Dongfang Jincheng (21st Century Business Herald, 16 Nov) and TrendForce (Q3 89.0, updated 31 Oct)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slipping again","url":"https://m.21jingji.com/article/20261116/herald/f32e9c05cac3398f9ea00907b7e4bfb2.html"},{"change":"+0.4 pt","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":-2.7},{"l":"Jan 26","v":-3.1},{"l":"Feb 26","v":-3.2},{"l":"Mar 26","v":-3.4},{"l":"Apr 26","v":-3.5},{"l":"May 26","v":-3.5},{"l":"Jun 26","v":-3.3},{"l":"Jul 26","v":-3.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":-3},{"l":"Sep 26","v":-2.8},{"l":"Oct 26","v":-2.4}],"latest":"−2.4%","name":"New Home Prices, 70 cities, y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"−2.8%","read":"The Reuters calculation on the NBS data has new-home prices down 2.4% y/y in October after −2.8%, the smallest fall since November 2025, and down 0.1% m/m for a fourth month at the same pace. Shanghai rose 2.7% y/y and was the only major city rising on both bases; Beijing fell 2.6%, Guangzhou 0.4% and Shenzhen 0.2%, with tier-one resale prices up an eighth month. Volumes are the other half: January to October new-home sales fell 13.7% by area and 14.3% by value, second-hand transactions rose 11.4%, and property investment fell 21.6%, so the price line is improving while the cycle that drives local-government revenue and commodity demand is still shrinking.","ref":0,"refLabel":"0 = flat prices","signal":"warn","signalWord":"40th monthly fall","src":"NBS (16 Nov) via Reuters on Investing.com and Trading Economics; NBS national economy release (sales, investment)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Decline narrowing","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economic-indicators/drop-in-chinas-new-home-prices-narrows-to-11month-low-5028306"}],"sub":"Forward-looking. Read these first.","title":"Leading indicators"},{"id":"coincident","rows":[{"change":"−0.7 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":4.9},{"l":"Nov 25","v":4.8},{"l":"Dec 25","v":5.2},{"l":"Feb 26","v":6.3},{"l":"Mar 26","v":5.7},{"l":"Apr 26","v":4.1},{"l":"May 26","v":4.5},{"l":"Jun 26","v":5.3},{"l":"Jul 26","v":4.5},{"l":"Aug 26","v":5.2},{"l":"Sep 26","v":5.5},{"l":"Oct 26","v":4.8}],"latest":"+4.8%","name":"Industrial Production, y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+5.5%","read":"Missed the 5.3% consensus and slowed 0.7 points from September; January to October is 5.3% and output rose 0.21% m/m. Manufacturing grew 5.4%, mining 0.7% and utilities 4.4%; high-tech manufacturing rose 17.6%, equipment 10.6% and computers and electronics 19.4%, while chemicals slowed to 1.3% and petroleum and coal processing fell for a sixth month on energy costs. Private firms grew 3.2% and state firms 2.1%, and export delivery value rose 18.6%, so production still tracks foreign demand. The NBS cited the Mid-Autumn holiday base and said domestic supply is strong and demand weak.","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Missed 5.3%, export-led","src":"NBS October release (16 Nov) via stats.gov.cn; People's Daily; Dongfang Jincheng via 21st Century Business Herald (consensus, sector detail)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slowest since July","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/zxfbhjd/202611/t20261116_1965844.html"},{"change":"−0.7 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":2.9},{"l":"Nov 25","v":1.3},{"l":"Dec 25","v":0.9},{"l":"Feb 26","v":2.8},{"l":"Mar 26","v":1.7},{"l":"Apr 26","v":0.2},{"l":"May 26","v":-0.6},{"l":"Jun 26","v":1},{"l":"Jul 26","v":0.6},{"l":"Aug 26","v":0.4},{"l":"Sep 26","v":1.1},{"l":"Oct 26","v":0.4}],"latest":"+0.4%","name":"Retail Sales, y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+1.1%","read":"Rose 0.4% y/y against a 0.8% consensus, back to the August low, and 0.02% m/m against a ten-year October average of 0.45%; CNY 4.646T in the month and +1.0% year to date. Goods rose 0.3% and catering 0.7%; autos fell 21.4%, gold and jewellery 27.7% and apparel 2.0%, telecom equipment slowed to 6.5% from 31.1% as last year's subsidy base arrived, appliances rose 2.5% and petroleum products 4.4% on fuel prices; sales at units above designated size fell 4.9%. Services retail is +4.9% year to date against goods +0.9%. Under the framework this is the domestic economy the official PMIs describe, with the trade-in subsidies fading and CAAM domestic vehicle sales −26.6%.","signal":"bad","signalWord":"Autos −21.4%","src":"NBS October release (16 Nov) via stats.gov.cn; Dongfang Jincheng via 21st Century Business Herald (categories, consensus)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Back to the August low","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/zxfbhjd/202611/t20261116_1965844.html"},{"change":"−0.9 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":-1.7},{"l":"Nov 25","v":-2.6},{"l":"Dec 25","v":-3.8},{"l":"Feb 26","v":1.8},{"l":"Mar 26","v":1.7},{"l":"Apr 26","v":-1.6},{"l":"May 26","v":-4.1},{"l":"Jun 26","v":-5.7},{"l":"Jul 26","v":-6.7},{"l":"Aug 26","v":-7.2},{"l":"Sep 26","v":-7.2},{"l":"Oct 26","v":-8.1}],"latest":"−8.1%","name":"Fixed Asset Investment, YTD y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Jan-Oct 2026","prior":"−7.2%","read":"Fell 8.1% y/y in January to October (CNY 36.48T) against a −6.9% to −7.0% consensus, deepening again after two months at −7.2%; October fell 2.93% m/m. Property development investment fell 21.6% (−20.6% through September), infrastructure 5.1% (−4.2%) and manufacturing 2.9% (−2.1%, autos −7.9%); private investment fell 11.4% and investment excluding property 5.1%, while intellectual-property products rose 9.2% and high-tech industry 4.0%. By sector primary fell 6.1%, secondary 3.6% and tertiary 10.9%. The September fiscal measures have not reached physical work; Dongfang Jincheng expects the infrastructure drag to narrow by year-end but property to deepen to about −22%.","ref":0,"refLabel":"0 = flat investment","signal":"bad","signalWord":"Property −21.6%, infrastructure −5.1%","src":"NBS October release (16 Nov) via stats.gov.cn; Dongfang Jincheng via 21st Century Business Herald (prior splits); EconoTimes (consensus)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Deepening again","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/zxfbhjd/202611/t20261116_1965844.html"},{"change":"−1.1 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":-1.1},{"l":"Nov 25","v":5.9},{"l":"Dec 25","v":6.6},{"l":"Feb 26","v":21.8},{"l":"Mar 26","v":2.5},{"l":"Apr 26","v":14.1},{"l":"May 26","v":19.4},{"l":"Jun 26","v":27},{"l":"Jul 26","v":23.9},{"l":"Aug 26","v":25},{"l":"Sep 26","v":36.3},{"l":"Oct 26","v":35.2}],"latest":"+35.2%","name":"Exports, y/y","next":"8 Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+36.3%","read":"Exports were $412.33B in October, up 35.2% y/y against a 33.5% consensus and 36.3% in September, helped by a low base (October 2025 was −1.2%); imports rose 41.6% to $307.05B against a 32% consensus, the fastest since May 2021, so the surplus narrowed to about $105.3B from $133.53B (consensus about $125.8B) and the January to October surplus is about $1.04T. Shipments to ASEAN rose 46.3%, to the EU 24.4% and to the US 32.9% with the US surplus about $33B; integrated-circuit exports were $39.594B (+137.1%), autos $19.692B (+37.6%), phones $17.569B (+13.2%) and rare earths 4,386.0 t after 4,269.8 t, while imports of integrated circuits rose 65.1%, copper ore 28.4% and crude 4.5% in value. The exporter side of the economy is still growing at a pace the official PMIs do not show, and the import jump is chips and commodity prices more than domestic demand; November trade is due 8 Dec.","signal":"good","signalWord":"Beat, imports +41.6%","src":"GAC via Trading Economics (exports, imports, US, EU and ASEAN), investinglive and AFP via the Jakarta Post (consensus, surplus), Sina Finance (Wang Qing, Zhang Di), Jiemian via Sina (chips, autos, phones, rare earths by value), FX168 (rare-earth tonnage), Zhitong via Investing.com (yuan terms)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slightly slower, still 35%","url":"https://tradingeconomics.com/china/exports-yoy"},{"change":"−0.1 pt","hist":[{"l":"Oct 25","v":5.1},{"l":"Nov 25","v":5.1},{"l":"Dec 25","v":5.1},{"l":"Feb 26","v":5.3},{"l":"Mar 26","v":5.4},{"l":"Apr 26","v":5.2},{"l":"May 26","v":5.1},{"l":"Jun 26","v":5},{"l":"Jul 26","v":5.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":5.3},{"l":"Sep 26","v":5.2},{"l":"Oct 26","v":5.1}],"latest":"5.1%","name":"Surveyed Urban Unemployment","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"5.2%","read":"Fell 0.1 point to 5.1%, matching October 2025, with the January to October average at 5.2%; the 31-city rate was 5.1%, local-registration workers 5.2%, migrants 4.9% (rural registration 4.8%) and the working week 48.3 hours. The September youth rate (16 to 24, ex-students) was 18%. Both PMI employment indexes are still below 50, so the rate is seasonal rather than a demand signal; it sits at the low end of the 5.0% to 5.4% range of the past three years.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"Same as a year ago","src":"NBS October release (16 Nov) via stats.gov.cn; People's Daily","trend":"down","trendWord":"Seasonal dip","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/zxfbhjd/202611/t20261116_1965844.html"},{"change":"+0.2 pt","hist":[{"l":"Q4 23","v":5.2},{"l":"Q1 24","v":5.3},{"l":"Q2 24","v":4.7},{"l":"Q3 24","v":4.6},{"l":"Q4 24","v":5.4},{"l":"Q1 25","v":5.4},{"l":"Q2 25","v":5.2},{"l":"Q3 25","v":4.8},{"l":"Q4 25","v":4.5},{"l":"Q1 26","v":5},{"l":"Q2 26","v":4.3},{"l":"Q3 26","v":4.5}],"latest":"+4.5%","name":"Real GDP, y/y","next":"Mid-Jan","period":"Q3 2026","prior":"+4.3%","read":"Beat the 4.4% Reuters consensus with 1.2% q/q (0.9% in Q2, consensus 1.1%), taking January to September to 4.6% and nominal GDP to CNY 107.1T; the secondary sector grew 3.8% year to date and services 5.2%. Growth is at the bottom of the 4.5% to 5.0% target range and rests on exports (September +29.6% in yuan terms) and high-tech output, with the NBS calling domestic demand \"insufficient\"; Capital Economics says the September data show the economy \"regained momentum\" while ANZ says fiscal support remains crucial. Q4 GDP is due in mid-January; a Q4 print at 4.4% or better delivers the year.","ref":5,"refLabel":"5% = top of 4.5-5% target","signal":"good","signalWord":"Bottom of target range","src":"NBS press release (19 Oct) via stats.gov.cn; investinglive; Business Recorder (Reuters)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Re-accelerating","url":"https://www.stats.gov.cn/english/PressRelease/202610/t20261019_1965619.html"}],"sub":"Confirmation of what the leading set signalled.","title":"Coincident indicators"},{"id":"policy","rows":[{"change":"−0.2 pt","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":0.7},{"l":"Dec 25","v":0.8},{"l":"Jan 26","v":0.2},{"l":"Feb 26","v":1.3},{"l":"Mar 26","v":1},{"l":"Apr 26","v":1.2},{"l":"May 26","v":1.2},{"l":"Jun 26","v":1},{"l":"Jul 26","v":0.5},{"l":"Aug 26","v":0.8},{"l":"Sep 26","v":0.9},{"l":"Oct 26","v":0.7}],"latest":"+0.7%","name":"CPI, y/y","next":"9 Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+0.9%","read":"Below the 0.8% consensus and flat m/m after +0.2% in September. Food fell 2.9% y/y with the decline widening 1.2 pt (pork −8.6%, fresh vegetables −16.9%, fresh fruit −3.8%, eggs +12.3%, beef +8.7%) and fell 1.0% m/m; non-food rose 1.5%, services 0.7% (−0.1 pt), consumer goods 0.8%, energy 9.9% after 7.3% with gasoline up 22.4% y/y (+0.63 pt), and storage devices, tablets, computers and phones added about 0.26 pt; industrial consumer goods ex-energy slowed to 1.2% from 1.6%. The NBS release does not give core CPI on the pages opened (September was 1.0%). The headline is oil pushing one way and food the other, with the January to October average at 0.9%; November CPI is due 9 Dec.","ref":0,"refLabel":"0 = deflation line","signal":"warn","signalWord":"Food −2.9%, below 1%","src":"NBS release (9 Nov) via Xinhua on Sina, CGTN and People's Daily; 21st Century Business Herald (components, analysts); investinglive (consensus)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Three-month low","url":"https://news.sina.com.cn/c/2026-11-09/doc-iniyazea3009558.shtml"},{"change":"+0.7 pt","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":-2.2},{"l":"Dec 25","v":-1.9},{"l":"Jan 26","v":-1.4},{"l":"Feb 26","v":-0.9},{"l":"Mar 26","v":0.5},{"l":"Apr 26","v":2.8},{"l":"May 26","v":3.9},{"l":"Jun 26","v":4.1},{"l":"Jul 26","v":3.5},{"l":"Aug 26","v":3.8},{"l":"Sep 26","v":5},{"l":"Oct 26","v":5.7}],"latest":"+5.7%","name":"PPI, y/y","next":"9 Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"+5.0%","read":"Above the 5.2% to 5.3% consensus and the fastest since mid-2022, but the m/m rise slowed to 0.7% from 1.2%. Oil and gas extraction rose 6.0% m/m, refined petroleum 6.8%, organic chemicals 6.8%, coal mining 2.7%, coal processing 3.2% and gas supply 1.5%, and those six sectors gave about 0.61 pt, more than 80% of the monthly rise; by sector coal mining is +36.6% y/y, oil and gas extraction +35.0%, fuel processing +29.9%, chemicals +16.4%, gas supply +7.9% and computer and electronic equipment +5.9%, and auto prices were flat m/m after three falls. Industrial input prices rose 7.9% y/y and 1.1% m/m; the January to October PPI is +2.7%. Analysts quoted by the 21st Century Business Herald say the gain is upstream profit recovery rather than chain-wide improvement, and CICC's Zhang Di says the PPI support to growth has peaked; with Brent at $92.57 on 9 Nov against October's highs above $100, the November cost-push is smaller. October profits on 27 Nov show whether downstream losses narrow.","ref":0,"refLabel":"0 = deflation line","signal":"good","signalWord":"Cost-push, margins squeezed","src":"NBS release (9 Nov) via CGTN and People's Daily; 21st Century Business Herald (sector detail, analysts); investinglive (consensus); Sina Finance (Zhang Di); Capp Notes (Brent)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Fastest since 2022, m/m slowing","url":"https://www.21jingji.com/article/20261109/herald/4b33606f08ee0a2dd4f51c5c52f037e5.html"},{"change":"−10 bp (May 2025)","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":3},{"l":"Jan 26","v":3},{"l":"Feb 26","v":3},{"l":"Mar 26","v":3},{"l":"Apr 26","v":3},{"l":"May 26","v":3},{"l":"Jun 26","v":3},{"l":"Jul 26","v":3},{"l":"Aug 26","v":3},{"l":"Sep 26","v":3},{"l":"Oct 26","v":3},{"l":"20 Nov","v":3}],"latest":"3.00%","name":"1-Year Loan Prime Rate","next":"21 Dec","period":"Since 20 May 2025","prior":"3.10%","read":"Held at 3.00% on 20 Nov for an 18th month, with the 5-year at 3.50%; the last change was the 10 bp cut of May 2025. Wang Qing of Dongfang Jincheng says bank net interest margins near historic lows give quoting banks no incentive to lower their spreads, reads the October miss as a normal monthly fluctuation with Q4 momentum still up, and expects a broad 10 to 20 bp cut in 2027 rather than soon; Dong Ximiao of Zhaolian says a small LPR fall is possible after the December Central Economic Work Conference. The PBoC eases through the instrument instead: the overnight reverse repo at 1.25% has been the main policy rate since 2 Nov, the buyback relending rate is 1.00%, new corporate loans priced at about 2.9% in October (−0.2 pt y/y) and new mortgages at about 3.1%, and the Q3 report pushes DR001-linked loan pricing. The next fixing is 21 Dec.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"18 months unchanged","src":"PBoC LPR announcement (20 Nov) via The Paper and China News Service; 21st Century Business Herald and Jiemian via Sohu (20 Nov: Wang Qing, Dong Ximiao, loan rates); Bank of China LPR table","trend":"flat","trendWord":"Held 20 Nov","url":"https://www.chinanews.com.cn/cj/2026/11-20/10735037.shtml"},{"change":"0 bp","hist":[],"latest":"1.40%","name":"7-Day Reverse Repo Rate","period":"24 Nov 2026","prior":"1.40%","read":"The 7-day rate is 1.40% and the overnight reverse repo at 1.25% has been the main policy rate since 2 Nov. On 24 Nov the PBoC lent CNY 516B overnight at 1.25% against CNY 499.5B maturing, a CNY 16.5B net injection, and after the close announced for 25 Nov a CNY 800B 1-year MLF against CNY 1T maturing (a CNY 200B reduction; with the CNY 300B cut in November's outright reverse repos the medium-term tools net a CNY 500B drain this month) plus a CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo, the first 7-day operation since the overnight rate became the anchor, on a day when CNY 516B of overnight repos and CNY 80B of treasury cash deposits also mature and reserves settle. Funding firmed a little: DR001 rose 1.18 bp to 1.2739%, DR007 2.57 bp to 1.3977%, above DR014 at 1.3768%, overnight Shibor 1.2 bp to 1.2740%, 7-day Shibor 2.3 bp to 1.3960%, 14-day 0.7 bp to 1.3770% and 3-month Shibor held at 1.4000%; state-bank NCDs were about 1.365% at 1 month (+1.5 bp), 1.405% at 3 months and 1.42% at 1 year (flat). Dong Ximiao of Zhaolian puts the week's liquidity needs near CNY 1.3T before operations and reads the 7-day as the cross-month fill, Ming Ming of CITIC says the mix met expectations and funding rates should ease back, and Wang Qing of Dongfang Jincheng puts the November DR001 mean at 1.29% against 1.39% in June to September and expects the medium-term tools to return to net injections. The PBoC also sold CNY 20B of 3-month bills at 1.32% and CNY 30B of 1-year bills at 1.41% in Hong Kong.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"DR001 2.4 bp off the anchor, MLF cut CNY 200B","src":"cnfin money market daily and 10jqka fixed-income daily (24 Nov: CNY 516B overnight operation, maturities, Shibor, DR001, DR007, DR014, NCDs, Hong Kong bill results); Sohu via Cailianshe, 10jqka via Securities Times and Sing Tao (24 Nov: the 25 Nov MLF and 7-day announcement, maturities, November outright repo reduction, Dong Ximiao, Ming Ming, Wang Qing, Wen Bin, Liu Yu, SWS); Xinhua via Economic Information Daily (25 Nov)","trend":"flat","trendWord":"Overnight 1.25% anchor; CNY 800B MLF and CNY 500B 7-day on 25 Nov","url":"https://www.cnfin.com/hb-lb/detail/20261124/4499734_1.html"},{"change":"+0.1 pt","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":8.5},{"l":"Dec 25","v":8.3},{"l":"Jan 26","v":8.2},{"l":"Feb 26","v":8.2},{"l":"Mar 26","v":7.9},{"l":"Apr 26","v":7.8},{"l":"May 26","v":7.7},{"l":"Jun 26","v":7.4},{"l":"Jul 26","v":7.4},{"l":"Aug 26","v":7.2},{"l":"Sep 26","v":7.1},{"l":"Oct 26","v":7.2}],"latest":"7.2%","name":"Total Social Financing, stock y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"7.1%","read":"TSF stock was CNY 469.16T at end-October, up 7.2% y/y after 7.1% in September, the first increase in 15 months. The October flow was CNY 1.15T against a Caixin consensus of CNY 1.28T and CNY 815B a year earlier; January to October TSF was CNY 28.61T, CNY 2.29T less than a year earlier, with government bonds CNY 11.49T, corporate bonds CNY 3.1T (+CNY 1.27T y/y) and loans to the real economy CNY 10.91T (−CNY 3.61T y/y). The pickup is bonds and the policy financing tool, not bank lending, which is why the read is a credit impulse without private demand.","signal":"good","signalWord":"First rise in 15 months, bond-led","src":"PBoC October financial statistics and TSF release (13 Nov) via Sina Finance, The Paper and 21st Century Business Herald; Dow Jones via MarketScreener (consensus); SMM","trend":"up","trendWord":"Decelerating","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/jjxw/2026-11-13/doc-iniyqsna8023513.shtml"},{"change":"−0.1 pt","hist":[{"l":"Nov 25","v":8},{"l":"Dec 25","v":8.5},{"l":"Jan 26","v":9},{"l":"Feb 26","v":9},{"l":"Mar 26","v":8.5},{"l":"Apr 26","v":8.6},{"l":"May 26","v":8.6},{"l":"Jun 26","v":8},{"l":"Jul 26","v":7.7},{"l":"Aug 26","v":7.5},{"l":"Sep 26","v":7.2},{"l":"Oct 26","v":7.1}],"latest":"7.1%","name":"M2, y/y","next":"Mid-Dec","period":"Oct 2026","prior":"7.2%","read":"M2 was CNY 359.06T, up 7.1% y/y after 7.2%, below the 7.2% to 7.3% consensus; M1 was CNY 116.9T, up 4.4%, and M0 rose 10.7%. New yuan loans fell CNY 100B in October (Caixin consensus +CNY 89.7B, CNY 220B a year earlier), the third contraction this year: households −CNY 430B, corporates −CNY 160B with bills −CNY 311.7B, non-banks +CNY 347B; outstanding loans grew 4.7% (4.8% in September). Deposits grew 7.7% with fiscal deposits up CNY 3.03T year to date. Money growth is slowing while government paper replaces bank credit.","signal":"warn","signalWord":"New cycle low, loans −CNY 100B","src":"PBoC October financial statistics report (13 Nov) via Sina Finance and The Paper; Dow Jones via MarketScreener (consensus); Sing Tao","trend":"down","trendWord":"Slowing","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/jjxw/2026-11-13/doc-iniyqsna8023513.shtml"}],"sub":"Tracker rows added when the China page was built. They are not part of our original indicator list.","title":"Inflation and policy"},{"id":"markets","rows":[{"change":"−0.35 bp on 24 Nov","hist":[{"l":"4 Nov","v":1.608},{"l":"5 Nov","v":1.604},{"l":"6 Nov","v":1.587},{"l":"9 Nov","v":1.587},{"l":"12 Nov","v":1.5958},{"l":"13 Nov","v":1.608},{"l":"16 Nov","v":1.63},{"l":"17 Nov","v":1.591},{"l":"18 Nov","v":1.588},{"l":"19 Nov","v":1.575},{"l":"23 Nov","v":1.5825},{"l":"24 Nov","v":1.5815}],"latest":"1.582%","name":"10-Year CGB Yield","period":"24 Nov (active 10-year bond, 16:03 report)","prior":"1.583% on 23 Nov","read":"The active 10-year bond (26 coupon bond 16) was 1.5815% at the 10jqka 16:03 report on 24 Nov, down 0.35 bp from the 1.5825% close of 23 Nov; no later close was published by the pages opened, so the point is a late-session level. The 30-year special bond quoted on 24 Nov is 26 ultra-long special 06 at 2.029% (−0.5 bp), a different bond from the 04 issue quoted at 2.061% on 23 Nov, and the 10-year CDB bond (26 CDB 05) rose 0.9 bp to 1.685%; the 30-year future closed 0.13% higher at 117.75, the 10-year 0.06% higher at 110.115, the 5-year 0.03% higher at 106.815 and the 2-year flat at 102.638. Bank capital paper kept cheapening, with 2-year ABC tier-2 paper up 1.06 bp to 1.84%. The market absorbed a CNY 16.5B net injection with DR001 at 1.2739% and DR007 at 1.3977%, and after the close the PBoC announced a CNY 800B MLF against CNY 1T maturing plus a CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo for 25 Nov; SWS reads the shrinking MLF as a signal against a one-way long-bond rally, Xingye's Liu Yu expects balanced-to-loose funding across month-end and Ming Ming of CITIC expects funding rates to ease once the package lands. Anhui sold 10-year bonds at 1.59% and 15-year at 1.87%, and the 30-year to 10-year spread is about 45 bp. The US 10-year fell 4.0 bp to 4.9038%, so the gap is about 332 bp. Under the framework duration keeps the anchor, the LPR hold and the consumer data behind it; the tests are 1.55% to 1.60% on the 10-year and DR001 within 5 bp of 1.25% through the 25 Nov operations and month-end.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"Holding the floor into a CNY 200B MLF cut","src":"10jqka fixed-income daily (24 Nov 16:03: 10-year 1.5815% −0.35 bp, 30-year 2.0290%, CDB 1.6850%, futures closes and % changes, bank capital paper, fix); cnfin money market daily (24 Nov: funding); 10jqka via Securities Times and Sohu via Cailianshe (24 Nov: the 25 Nov MLF and 7-day announcement, SWS, Liu Yu, Ming Ming); Eastmoney financial breakfast (25 Nov: US Treasuries, dollar index)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Flat near 1.58%","url":"http://news.10jqka.com.cn/20261124/c682151415.shtml"},{"change":"+0.14% on 24 Nov","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":4629.94},{"l":"Jan 26","v":4706.34},{"l":"Feb 26","v":4710.65},{"l":"Mar 26","v":4450.05},{"l":"Apr 26","v":4807.31},{"l":"May 26","v":4892.12},{"l":"Jun 26","v":4979.43},{"l":"Jul 26","v":4588.2},{"l":"Aug 26","v":4625.09},{"l":"Sep 26","v":4357.62},{"l":"Oct 26","v":3985.5},{"l":"24 Nov","v":3963.82}],"latest":"3,963.82","name":"CSI 300","period":"24 Nov close","prior":"3,958.29 on 23 Nov","read":"The CSI 300 closed at 3,963.82 on 24 Nov, up 5.53 points or 0.14%, 5.68 points above the 23 Oct low of 3,958.14 and 6.0% below the 4,217.68 reversal line, in a session that opened strong and faded: the Shanghai Composite opened at 3,567.84, reached 3,585.22 and closed at 3,548.37 (+0.27%), the ChiNext opened more than 3% higher at 2,368.70, rose more than 4% at the peak and closed 0.05% lower at 2,278.99, its low of the day, the Shenzhen Component fell 0.29% to 10,423.60, the STAR 50 rose 1.81% to 1,250.09, the SSE 50 0.45% and the CSI 2000 0.23%, while the CSI 1000 fell 0.23% and the BSE 50 0.22%. Two-exchange turnover rose CNY 102.2B or 6.58% to CNY 1,655.1B, but breadth reversed to 1,952 up against 3,498 down with 64 limit-ups and 4 limit-downs. Defence (+1.52%), electronics (+1.51%) and machinery (+0.49%) led on physical AI, while nonferrous metals (−2.53%), oil and petrochemicals (−1.94%) and environmental (−1.34%) fell; Innolight and Eoptolink opened 10% and 8% higher and closed lower, Industrial Fulian rose 6.97% on a CNY 13.29B dividend, Victory Giant 6.27% and Ping An 2.20%, and Zijin fell 4.33%. Main funds were a net CNY 5.99B in (CSI 300 CNY 4.59B); the two-exchange margin balance was CNY 2,134.81B on 23 Nov (−CNY 8.99B) and ETFs took a net CNY 7.41B on 23 Nov. Hengsheng Qianhai's Long Jiangwei says a rebound needs volume and inflows, Everbright's Zhang Yusheng says long-term capital can stabilise the index and JPMorgan puts Asian positioning in the lowest 10% of history. Under the framework two small gains on fading breadth with the index sitting on its October low and copper breaking 5% keep the signal bad; the reversal test is a close above 4,217.68 on turnover back toward CNY 2T.","signal":"bad","signalWord":"6.0% below the reversal line, 3,498 fallers","src":"FX168 flash (24 Nov: CSI 300 3,963.82, +5.53, +0.14%; Shanghai, Shenzhen, ChiNext, STAR 50 closes), matching Jin10 via NewsNow; China Securities Journal via ce.cn and agudashi (24 Nov: index % changes, open levels, turnover CNY 1,655.1B +CNY 102.2B, breadth, Shenwan sectors, named stocks, main-fund flows, analysts); Tencent daily kline for the Shanghai Composite (open, high, low); 10jqka financial breakfast (25 Nov: margin balance 23 Nov, ETF flows 23 Nov); nbd.com.cn (24 Nov: Huaxia CSI 300 ETF constituents)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Second small gain, breadth faded","url":"https://www.fx168news.com/express/fastnews/1474719"},{"change":"−0.73% on 24 Nov","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":25630.54},{"l":"Jan 26","v":27387.11},{"l":"Feb 26","v":26630.54},{"l":"Mar 26","v":24788.14},{"l":"Apr 26","v":25776.53},{"l":"May 26","v":25182.39},{"l":"Jun 26","v":22881.02},{"l":"Jul 26","v":25884.43},{"l":"Aug 26","v":25566.99},{"l":"Sep 26","v":24613.27},{"l":"Oct 26","v":23294.42},{"l":"24 Nov","v":22219.65}],"latest":"22,219.65","name":"Hang Seng","period":"24 Nov close","prior":"22,383.74 on 23 Nov","read":"The Hang Seng opened 243 points higher at 22,627.29, reached 22,647.50 and closed 164.09 points or 0.73% lower at 22,219.65 on 24 Nov, its lowest close in more than 18 months and a sixth straight fall worth more than 1,500 points, on HK$212.63B against HK$253.09B on 23 Nov; the tech index fell 1.17% to 3,466.87, a more than two-year low below 3,500, the HSCEI 1.0% to 7,452.56 and the red-chip index 1.22% to 3,704.74. Xiaomi fell 3.71% to HK$26.5 before reporting Q3 revenue of CNY 107.24B, down 5.2% y/y, Meituan 3.31% to HK$64.2, Zhipu 6.23% to HK$319, MiniMax 2.8%, NetEase 2.2%, Kuaishou 1.84%, Baidu 1.81%, Alibaba 1.02% to HK$82.2 and Tencent 0.7% to HK$341.6; PetroChina fell 3.82%, Sinopec 3.13%, CNOOC 1.97%, China Hongqiao 4.9% (the worst blue chip) and Chalco more than 4% on the metals break, ICBC 1.09% and CCB 0.58%; Lenovo rose 3.70% (the best blue chip), XPeng 2.86%, Hua Hong 1.55%, Ping An 1.01%, HSBC 0.77%, Bank of China 0.73%, SMIC 0.5% and HKEX 0.34%; Public Financial Holdings rose more than 76% after shareholders approved Public Bank's HK$2.50 privatisation and Xiantong Pharma fell more than 23% on debut. Southbound investors bought a net HK$6.20B, led by Xiaomi (HK$1.09B) and Hua Hong (HK$0.94B) with CNOOC sold HK$0.52B, taking November to a net HK$21.70B after October's roughly HK$28B outflow (Wind via China Securities Journal; Securities Times prints HK$8.57B for the day on a page that could not be opened). Huatai's Yi Huan sees room for a technical bounce of uncertain durability, Soochow's Chen Meng stays defensive, CICC's Liu Gang compares the setup to the second half of 2023 and CITIC warns that US overnight trading would divert money from Hong Kong tech and consumer names; the index review widening the tech index to 50 stocks takes effect on 7 Dec. Under the framework a sixth fall to an 18-month low with the tech index at a two-year low is bad; a close back above 24,000 on southbound buying would change the read.","signal":"bad","signalWord":"Tech index 3,466.87, a two-year low","src":"Xinhua (24 Nov: close, points, turnover HK$212.633B, named stock closes); FX168 flash and 21st Century Business Herald (24 Nov: index closes, red chips); Tencent hkHSI daily kline (open, high, low); VOCO via Tiger and Sina (24 Nov: open, high, low, sixth fall, 18-month low, Xiaomi, CITIC, CSC); Tiger Brokers (24 Nov: constituent % moves, sectors); Titanium Media via Sohu (24 Nov: southbound HK$6.204B, Xiaomi, Hua Hong, CNOOC); China Securities Journal via 21st Century Business Herald (25 Nov: November-to-date flows, Yi Huan, Chen Meng, Liu Gang); National Business Daily via 21st Century Business Herald (24 Nov: Public Financial Holdings, HSCEI and tech constituents)","trend":"down","trendWord":"Sixth fall, lowest close in 18 months","url":"http://www.xinhuanet.com/20261124/860759fa1b254325a2af738ecd1108d6/c.html"},{"change":"+0.27% on 24 Nov","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":3968.84},{"l":"Jan 26","v":4117.95},{"l":"Feb 26","v":4162.88},{"l":"Mar 26","v":3891.86},{"l":"Apr 26","v":4112.16},{"l":"May 26","v":4068.57},{"l":"Jun 26","v":4094.4},{"l":"Jul 26","v":3832.26},{"l":"Aug 26","v":3986.3},{"l":"Sep 26","v":3842.19},{"l":"Oct 26","v":3599.02},{"l":"24 Nov","v":3548.37}],"latest":"3,548.37","name":"Shanghai Composite","period":"24 Nov close","prior":"3,538.95 on 23 Nov","read":"The Shanghai Composite opened at 3,567.84 on 24 Nov, reached 3,585.22, fell to 3,539.01 and closed at 3,548.37, up 9.42 points or 0.27%, on Shanghai turnover of CNY 771.9B; it is 47.5 points above the 3,500.83 52-week low of 20 Nov and 50.7 points below its October close of 3,599.02. The Shenzhen Component fell 0.29% to 10,423.60 after a midday 10,550.87, the ChiNext opened more than 3% higher at 2,368.70, rose more than 4% at the peak and closed 0.05% lower at 2,278.99, its low of the day, the STAR 50 rose 1.81% to 1,250.09 and the BSE 50 fell 0.22%, with 1,952 up, 3,498 down, 64 limit-ups and 4 limit-downs on two-exchange turnover of CNY 1,655.1B (+CNY 102.2B); the CSI bank index opened 1.08% lower and closed 0.35% higher. Physical AI, smart speakers, inverters, film and energy metals led (Tengyuan Cobalt +14.23%, Anpulong, Hengho Precision and Keli Sensor at the limit), precious metals, rare earths, coal and glass fell. Hu Xijin wrote that every A-share investor was disappointed by the fade; Banxia's Li Bei said she has gone long broad-index A-shares. Under the framework a high-open low-close with seven in ten stocks down, a day after the package rally, is bad; the index needs a close back above 3,599.02 on rising turnover to change the read.","signal":"bad","signalWord":"3,498 fallers, 47.5 points off a 52-week low","src":"Tencent daily kline for sh000001 (24 Nov: open 3,567.84, high 3,585.22, low 3,539.01, close 3,548.37, +9.42, +0.27%); FX168 flash and agudashi (24 Nov: closes, turnover by exchange, breadth, midday levels); China Securities Journal via ce.cn (24 Nov: sectors, limit counts, named stocks); Sina hourly reports (24 Nov: bank index, named stocks, Hu Xijin, Li Bei)","trend":"up","trendWord":"Opened at 3,567.84, faded, ChiNext −0.05%","url":"https://agudashi.com/5035.html"},{"change":"+0.01% on 24 Nov","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":6.9876},{"l":"Jan 26","v":6.952},{"l":"Feb 26","v":6.861},{"l":"Mar 26","v":6.8933},{"l":"Apr 26","v":6.8266},{"l":"May 26","v":6.7662},{"l":"Jun 26","v":6.7854},{"l":"Jul 26","v":6.7528},{"l":"Aug 26","v":6.7202},{"l":"Sep 26","v":6.7045},{"l":"Oct 26","v":6.6557},{"l":"24 Nov","v":6.6648}],"latest":"6.6648","name":"USD/CNY","period":"24 Nov","prior":"6.6643 on 23 Nov","read":"The onshore yuan closed at 6.6648 per dollar at 16:30 on 24 Nov, 5 pips weaker, after a fix set 9 pips stronger at 6.7111, with the offshore rate 21 pips stronger at 6.6647 at 18:00 (6-month swap −977 pips, 1-year −2,001); the 25 Nov fix was set 23 pips stronger at 6.7088, while the dollar index fell 0.48% to 103.814, the euro rose 0.57% to 1.0966, USD/JPY rose 0.16% to 159.21 and the US 10-year fell 4.0 bp to 4.9038%. The PBoC sold CNY 50B of Hong Kong bills (3-month at 1.32%, 1-year at 1.41%) and the spot rate has held between 6.6643 and 6.6735 for eight sessions with the fix moving 6.7088 to 6.7131, a counter-cyclical gap near 440 pips. Under the framework the yuan is a managed drift inside 6.65 to 6.70 with the 7.0 and 7.3 lines far away; a fix below 6.70 or a close above 6.70 would change the read.","signal":"neutral","signalWord":"Range 6.65 to 6.70","src":"FX168 flash (24 Nov 16:32: close 6.6648, −5 pips) and Eastmoney financial breakfast (25 Nov: onshore close, offshore 6.6647 at 18:00, swaps, dollar index 103.814, US Treasuries); 10jqka (24 Nov fix 6.7111, +9 pips); China News Service, MoneyDJ and SMM (25 Nov fix 6.7088, 23 pips stronger); cnfin (24 Nov: Hong Kong bill results); Xinhua Finance via Eastmoney (25 Nov: EUR, JPY)","trend":"up","trendWord":"5 pips weaker, fix 6.7088 on 25 Nov","url":"https://www.fx168news.com/express/fastnews/1474759"},{"change":"−$664 on 24 Nov (LME close)","hist":[{"l":"Dec 25","v":12504},{"l":"Jan 26","v":13369.5},{"l":"Feb 26","v":13439.5},{"l":"Mar 26","v":12160},{"l":"Apr 26","v":13015.5},{"l":"May 26","v":13615},{"l":"Jun 26","v":13341},{"l":"Jul 26","v":13834},{"l":"Aug 26","v":14535},{"l":"Sep 26","v":14487},{"l":"Oct 26","v":14449},{"l":"24 Nov","v":11826}],"latest":"$11,826","name":"Copper, LME","period":"24 Nov LME close (Eastmoney)","prior":"$12,165 on 23 Nov (cash settlement)","read":"LME copper closed $664 or 5.31% lower at $11,826 a tonne on 24 Nov on the Eastmoney breakfast table, giving back Monday's bounce and more; Fastmarkets had the 3-month contract at $11,858.50 at 15:45 London, down 5.05%, below $12,000 for the first time in 11 months, with LME stocks up 6,850 t on the morning and the Yangshan import premium off its $500 record to $450. Westmetall has now posted the 23 Nov cash settlement at $12,165 (3-month $12,170, stocks 330,975 t), so the prior is the settlement basis and the latest is the evening-close basis; the 24 Nov settlement was not posted at this refresh and will replace the point. Tin fell 7.25% to $39,539, aluminium 3.08% to $2,769, zinc 3.43% to $3,432 and nickel to $15,166, while cobalt rose 14.96% to $38,540 on the DRC export suspension from 30 Nov. Fastmarkets' Andy Farida cites the stronger dollar earlier in the month, the AI-trade sell-off and the US mid-term result, and the WSJ report that the US is preparing higher tariffs on dozens of countries; ING calls the fall a financial-market story with Chinese physical tightness intact. The demand side is the 16 Nov data: property investment −21.6% year to date, infrastructure −5.1%, cement output −1.3% and CAAM domestic vehicle sales −26.6%, against copper-ore imports +28.4% and electronics output +19.4%. Under the framework the demand gauge is bad until the price is back above $14,000 with stocks falling.","signal":"bad","signalWord":"16% below 9 Nov, stocks rising","src":"Eastmoney financial breakfast (25 Nov: LME closes for 24 Nov, copper −$664 to $11,826, aluminium, zinc, nickel, tin, cobalt); Fastmarkets (24 Nov 17:09: 3-month prices at 15:45, stocks, Yangshan premium, Farida, ING); Westmetall (LME cash settlement, 3-month and stocks to 23 Nov; no 24 Nov row posted at this refresh); Trading Economics (24 Nov: 11-month low)","trend":"down","trendWord":"−5.31%, an 11-month low","url":"https://finance.eastmoney.com/a/202611243938774940.html"},{"change":"0.00% on 24 Nov","hist":[],"latest":"$90.67/t","name":"Iron Ore","period":"24 Nov","prior":"$90.67/t on 23 Nov","read":"Quoted at $90.67 a tonne for 24 Nov (62% Fe CFR Tianjin), unchanged on the day per Trading Economics, down 0.12% on the month and 13.24% on the year, with the page updated 25 Nov; the quote has sat at $90.67 since 20 Nov while LME copper fell 5.31% on 24 Nov. The demand side is the 16 Nov data: property investment −21.6% and infrastructure −5.1% year to date (Western Securities puts October property investment alone at −33.2%), new-home sales area −13.7%, cement output −1.3% and the construction PMI at 48.0 with construction new orders 40.0; Vanke's MTN004 goes to an extension vote on 8 Dec and R&F's restructuring proposal failed. The $90 line is the next test; a return above $95 or a construction PMI above 50 would change the read.","signal":"bad","signalWord":"Property investment −21.6%, below $92","src":"Trading Economics (24 Nov quote, daily, monthly and yearly change; page last updated 25 Nov); NBS October release (16 Nov); Jiemian via Sina and Vanke's HK filing via Sina (24 Nov: MTN004 holder meeting); 21st Century Business Herald bond brief (24 Nov: R&F)","trend":"flat","trendWord":"Flat at $90.67","url":"https://tradingeconomics.com/commodity/iron-ore"}],"sub":"Additions to the leading and coincident core. Closes for Monday 19 Oct in the mainland, copper and iron ore; Hong Kong was closed on 19 Oct, so the Hang Seng is the 16 Oct close and 20 Oct figures in the text are midday levels.","title":"Market readings"}],"takeaways":["The large caps gained and the tape faded. The CSI 300 closed at 3,963.82 on 24 Nov, up 5.53 points or 0.14%, 5.68 points above the 23 Oct low of 3,958.14 and 6.0% below the 4,217.68 reversal line; the Shanghai Composite opened at 3,567.84, reached 3,585.22 and closed at 3,548.37 (+0.27%), the ChiNext opened at 2,368.70, more than 3% higher, rose more than 4% at the peak and closed 0.05% lower at 2,278.99, the Shenzhen Component fell 0.29% to 10,423.60, the STAR 50 rose 1.81% to 1,250.09 (science and technology composite +1.16%), the SSE 50 rose 0.45%, the CSI 1000 fell 0.23%, the CSI 2000 rose 0.23% and the BSE 50 fell 0.22%. Two-exchange turnover rose CNY 102.2B or 6.58% to CNY 1,655.1B (Shanghai CNY 771.9B, Shenzhen CNY 883.2B; 10jqka's whole-market figure is CNY 1,667.8B, +CNY 103.8B), but breadth reversed from Monday's 4,600 advancers to 1,952 up, 3,498 down, 64 limit-ups and 4 limit-downs, with 255 stocks up more than 5% and 44 down more than 5%. Defence (+1.52%), electronics (+1.51%) and machinery (+0.49%) led on physical AI, smart speakers and inverters; nonferrous metals (−2.53%), oil and petrochemicals (−1.94%) and environmental (−1.34%) fell with precious metals, rare earths and coal, Zhaojin and Western Gold about −5%; Innolight opened more than 10% higher and Eoptolink 8% and both closed lower, Industrial Fulian rose 6.97% on a CNY 13.29B interim dividend and Tengyuan Cobalt rose 14.23% on the DRC export suspension. Main funds were a net CNY 5.99B in (CSI 300 CNY 4.59B; electronics CNY 6.42B, communications CNY 1.79B; computers −CNY 1.55B, non-bank financials −CNY 0.99B). The two-exchange margin balance was CNY 2,134.81B on 23 Nov, down CNY 8.99B, a day before the 30 Nov ratio cut; ETFs took a net CNY 7.41B on 23 Nov. Hengsheng Qianhai's Long Jiangwei says incremental money is thin and a rebound needs volume and inflows; Everbright's Zhang Yusheng says long-term capital can stabilise the market; JPMorgan puts Asian investor positioning in the lowest 10% of history for a fourth week.","Hong Kong fell a sixth day to an 18-month low while southbound money came back. The Hang Seng opened 243 points higher at 22,627.29, reached 22,647.50 and closed 164.09 points or 0.73% lower at 22,219.65, its lowest close in more than 18 months and more than 1,500 points below where it stood six sessions ago, on HK$212.63B against HK$253.09B on Monday; the tech index fell 1.17% to 3,466.87, a more than two-year low below 3,500, the HSCEI 1.0% to 7,452.56 and the red-chip index 1.22% to 3,704.74. Xiaomi fell 3.71% to HK$26.5 before reporting Q3 revenue of CNY 107.24B, down 5.2% y/y (smartphones CNY 45.6B, EVs and AI CNY 23.9B), Meituan fell 3.31%, Zhipu 6.23% to HK$319, MiniMax 2.8%, NetEase 2.2%, Kuaishou 1.84%, Baidu 1.81%, Alibaba 1.02% to HK$82.2 and Tencent 0.7% to HK$341.6, PetroChina fell 3.82%, Sinopec 3.13%, CNOOC 1.97%, China Hongqiao 4.9% and Chalco more than 4% with ICBC −1.09% and CCB −0.58%, while Lenovo rose 3.70%, XPeng 2.86%, Hua Hong 1.55%, Ping An 1.01%, HSBC 0.77%, Bank of China 0.73%, SMIC 0.5% and HKEX 0.34%, Public Financial Holdings rose more than 76% after shareholders approved Public Bank's HK$2.50 privatisation, and Xiantong Pharma fell more than 23% on its H-share debut. Southbound investors bought a net HK$6.20B, led by Xiaomi (HK$1.09B) and Hua Hong (HK$0.94B) with CNOOC sold HK$0.52B, taking November to a net HK$21.70B of inflows after October's HK$28B outflow and the year to about HK$430B (Wind via China Securities Journal); Securities Times prints HK$8.57B for the day, which could not be opened. Huatai's Yi Huan calls the technicals extreme enough for a bounce of uncertain durability, Soochow's Chen Meng stays defensive, CICC's Liu Gang compares the market to the second half of 2023 and puts mid-2027 as the observation point, CSC expects liquidity to improve in 2027 and CITIC warns that US overnight trading would divert money from Hong Kong tech and consumer names; after the close the index review widening the tech index to 50 stocks takes effect on 7 Dec.","The PBoC trimmed the MLF and added a 7-day backstop. On 24 Nov the PBoC lent CNY 516B overnight at 1.25% against CNY 499.5B maturing, a CNY 16.5B net injection, and sold CNY 20B of 3-month bills at 1.32% and CNY 30B of 1-year bills at 1.41% in Hong Kong; after the close it announced for 25 Nov a CNY 800B 1-year MLF (fixed quantity, rate tender, multiple prices) against CNY 1T maturing, a CNY 200B reduction that with the CNY 300B cut in November's two outright reverse repo tenors makes a CNY 500B medium-term net drain for the month, plus a CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo, the first 7-day operation since the overnight rate became the anchor on 2 Nov, on a day when CNY 516B of overnight repos and CNY 80B of treasury cash deposits also mature and reserves settle. Funding firmed a little into the announcement: DR001 rose 1.18 bp to 1.2739%, DR007 2.57 bp to 1.3977% (above DR014 at 1.3768%), overnight Shibor 1.2 bp to 1.2740%, 7-day Shibor 2.3 bp to 1.3960% and 3-month Shibor held at 1.4000%, with state-bank NCDs at about 1.365% (1-month, +1.5 bp) to 1.42% (1-year, flat). Dong Ximiao of Zhaolian puts the week's liquidity drain near CNY 1.3T before PBoC operations and reads the 7-day as filling the cross-month gap, Ming Ming of CITIC says the mix met expectations and funding rates should ease back from a November DR001 centre near 1.3% and DR007 near 1.4%, Wang Qing of Dongfang Jincheng puts the November DR001 mean at 1.29% against 1.39% in June to September and expects the MLF and outright repos to return to net injections, Wen Bin of Minsheng says the policy rate matters more than tool usage, Xingye's Liu Yu expects balanced-to-loose funding across month-end and SWS reads the shrinking MLF as a signal against a one-way long-bond rally. The active 10-year CGB was 1.5815% at the 16:03 report, down 0.35 bp, the 30-year (26 ultra-long special 06) 2.029% (−0.5 bp) and the 10-year CDB bond 1.685% (+0.9 bp); the 30-year future rose 0.13% to 117.75, the 10-year 0.06% to 110.115, the 5-year 0.03% to 106.815 and the 2-year was flat at 102.638. Anhui sold 7-year bonds at 1.44%, 10-year at 1.59% and 15-year at 1.87%. The fix was set 9 pips stronger at 6.7111 on 24 Nov and 23 pips stronger at 6.7088 on 25 Nov, the onshore yuan closed 5 pips weaker at 6.6648 at 16:30 with the offshore rate 21 pips stronger at 6.6647 at 18:00, as the dollar index fell 0.48% to 103.814, USD/JPY rose to 159.21 and the US 10-year fell 4.0 bp to 4.9038%, a gap to the CGB of about 332 bp.","Trade got a two-month extension and politics got a Politburo case. MOFCOM announced on 24 Nov that the second paragraph of its Announcement 2024 No. 46 (no export licences for gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard-material dual-use items to the US, stricter end-use review for graphite) is suspended from 28 Nov 2026 to 27 Jan 2027, extending the pause agreed in November 2025 that was due to lapse this week, with no US step reported in return and the rare-earth pause separately dated to 10 Jan; the same day the European Commission issued a preliminary finding in its hybrid-vehicle safeguard case with temporary measures from 1 Dec and MOFCOM reserved the right to WTO dispute settlement and trade compensation, unnamed sources told US media the administration is preparing to raise tariffs on dozens of countries and that USTR Greer may announce an industrial-subsidy investigation covering the EU as soon as this week, and VOCO reports Commerce added Alibaba's Singapore unit Apex Enterprise Solutions and six other entities to the entity list, with Alibaba saying Apex never transferred controlled chips. Xinhua reported that Chen Jining, Politburo member and Shanghai party secretary, is under CCDI investigation for suspected serious violations of discipline and law. Also on 24 Nov: Vanke's 22 Vanke MTN004 (CNY 1.199B outstanding, principal due 15 Dec) goes to a second holder meeting on 8 Dec on extension terms (record date 7 Dec, vote by 10 Dec); R&F's H16 R&F 5 holders approved a grace period while the restructuring proposal failed; NAFMII disciplined five issuers including Tianjin Real Estate Group and China Minsheng Investment and barred Guanghui Auto from the market for two years; Shenzhen regulators met 40 listed companies to push buybacks and insider purchases, Qinghai Salt Lake proposed a CNY 1.5B to 2B buyback for cancellation and Innolight CNY 2B to 4B; MIIT approved 6G pilots in eight provinces; the NEA put October power consumption at 870.9 TWh, +1.6% y/y; Bilibili's Q3 revenue rose 8% to CNY 8.32B; Shenzhou-24 was set to launch at 08:18 on 25 Nov with the first foreign (Pakistani) crew member.","Semiconductors and copper gave Monday back. The Philadelphia semiconductor index fell 7.88% on 24 Nov with all 30 members lower, Nvidia −5.86% to $155.38 after its 31.48% Monday, Micron −11.01%, SanDisk −11.13%, AMD −8.86%, Intel −8.15%, Arm −8.55%, TSMC −3.83% and SK Hynix −9.9% after Goldman cut its 2028 DRAM and NAND price forecasts by about 20%; the Nasdaq fell 1.48% to 23,733.54 and the S&P 500 0.50% to 7,201.09 while the Dow rose 0.85% to 50,018.70 on Nike (+5.89%), Walmart and Apple (+1.43%), the Golden Dragon index rose 0.12% with Alibaba's ADR −1.37%, and Conference Board consumer confidence jumped 11.4 points to 103.3 against 92.5 expected as gasoline fell a 31st day to about $3.60; the US 10-year fell 4.0 bp to 4.9038%, the 2-year to 4.6705% and the dollar index 0.48% to 103.814, with the Fed's discount-rate minutes showing eight of twelve reserve banks asked for a hike to 4.25% and the December hike priced near 97%. Asia had already run on Monday's Nvidia move: the Nikkei rose 3.91% to 58,644.63 and the Kospi 6.32% to 5,006.03, while the DAX fell 1.26% and the Euro Stoxx 50 1.16%. LME copper fell $664 or 5.31% to $11,826 on the Eastmoney close basis (Fastmarkets: 3-month $11,858.50 at 15:45 London, −5.05%, an 11-month low below $12,000, with stocks up 6,850 t on the morning and the Yangshan premium off its $500 record to $450; ING calls it a financial-market story with Chinese physical tightness intact), after Westmetall posted the 23 Nov cash settlement at $12,165 (3-month $12,170, stocks 330,975 t); tin fell 7.25% to $39,539, aluminium 3.08% to $2,769 and zinc 3.43% to $3,432 while cobalt rose 14.96% to $38,540 on the DRC ban. WTI settled 2.35% higher at $82.05 and Brent 2.27% higher at $91.40 as the IRGC said Hormuz stays closed until Iran's seven conditions are met, COMEX gold fell 2.78% to $3,550.00 and silver 6.10% to $40.54, and iron ore was flat at $90.67. Nothing on the Chinese data calendar printed; the growth score stays at 40, inflation at 48, policy at 60, and the markets score moves down 2 to 25 on the faded breadth, the sixth Hang Seng fall, the semiconductor reversal and the copper break, with the posture Risk-off."],"translation":[{"body":"The CSI 300 closed at 3,963.82 on 24 Nov, up 0.14% and 5.68 points above the October low it reclaimed on Monday, but the session opened strong and faded: the ChiNext gave up a 4% intraday gain to close 0.05% lower at its low of the day, breadth reversed to 1,952 up against 3,498 down even as two-exchange turnover rose 6.6% to CNY 1,655.1B, the metals and oil names that led on Monday's rotation were sold and the margin balance fell CNY 8.99B to CNY 2,134.81B on 23 Nov ahead of the 30 Nov ratio cut. Hong Kong fell a sixth day to an 18-month closing low with the tech index at a two-year low below 3,500, Xiaomi down 3.71% before a 5.2% revenue decline and the semiconductor complex in New York down 7.88% overnight. Under the framework two small large-cap gains on fading breadth with the Hang Seng making new lows and copper breaking 5% do not change a Risk-off posture; the reversal test is a CSI 300 close above 4,217.68 on turnover back toward CNY 2T, and the next demand test is the 30 Nov PMIs on the day the margin ratio falls to 80%.","title":"Equities"},{"body":"The active 10-year CGB was 1.5815% at the 16:03 report on 24 Nov, down 0.35 bp, with the 30-year at 2.029%, the 10-year future up 0.06% and bank capital paper still cheapening, as DR001 rose 1.18 bp to 1.2739% and DR007 2.57 bp to 1.3977%; after the close the PBoC announced a CNY 800B MLF against CNY 1T maturing plus a CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo for 25 Nov, which SWS reads as a signal against a one-way long-bond rally and Ming Ming of CITIC reads as enough to ease funding back. The yuan closed 5 pips weaker at 6.6648 with the offshore rate at 6.6647, the fix was set 23 pips stronger at 6.7088 on 25 Nov, and the dollar index fell 0.48% to 103.814 with the US 10-year at 4.9038%, a gap of about 332 bp. Under the framework the anchor at 1.25%, the CPI at 0.7% and the consumer data hold the 10-year in a 1.55% to 1.60% range, the MLF reduction is a quantity choice at an unchanged price, and the currency is a managed drift inside 6.65 to 6.70; a 10-year close above 1.60% or DR001 more than 5 bp above 1.25% through month-end would change the read.","title":"Fixed income and currency"},{"body":"The PBoC put a net CNY 16.5B in overnight on 24 Nov and set up 25 Nov as the month-end test: CNY 800B of MLF against CNY 1T maturing, a CNY 500B 7-day reverse repo, CNY 516B of overnight repos and CNY 80B of treasury deposits maturing and reserves settling, with the medium-term tools netting a CNY 500B drain for November; Wang Qing expects them to return to net injections and Dong Ximiao reads the mix as the short end managing the floor and the middle managing the pace. The LPR was held at 3.00% and 3.50% on 20 Nov for an 18th month, the 22 Nov equity package (margin ratio 80% from 30 Nov, ChiNext market-making, more than CNY 4.6B of fee relief) is leverage and cost rather than demand, and Shenzhen regulators spent 24 Nov pushing 40 listed companies toward buybacks. On the external side MOFCOM extended the suspension of the gallium, germanium, antimony and superhard-material export ban to the US from 28 Nov to 27 Jan 2027, the EU moved to temporary hybrid-vehicle safeguards from 1 Dec and US media report tariff increases on dozens of countries in preparation; on the political side Shanghai party secretary Chen Jining, a Politburo member, was placed under CCDI investigation. Under the framework the stance stays Easing by instrument and the policy score stays at 60: the toolkit and the anchor are intact, the cross-month backstop is in place, and the demand-side package is still missing into the 30 Nov PMIs and the December meetings.","title":"Liquidity and policy"}]};
